''               R1-T0-EXHAUST are BOOL cells (measured TRUE/FALSE = every condition ANDed), so
''               no record can print an in-band number beside a FAIL.
''               14 Sep 2026 -- task 3537 T0 follow-ups: SF_RESTART_HI / SF_EXHAUST_HI removed (unused
''               since the BOOL change), and every sign-off cell prints NOMEAS,n,0 when a trapped
''               call it judges aborted (design SS H.1), found by a completion flag, not the trap's
''               value -- R4-T0-1M-TICKS, R1-T0-START/RESTART/EXHAUST, R8-T0-ZXS, R3-T0-STOPPED,
''               R2-T0-REPEAT/DIRTY/EMPTY and R10-T0-STOPREADY.
''               14 Sep 2026 -- task 3539 (PL-44/PL-47): removed every trap used to capture a
''               normal return -- start()/testSetup()/stopAfterDistance() are now called
''               UNTRAPPED throughout and judged by their returned value. A trap remains only for
''               T0-6's getRotationCount(99)/stopAfterDistance(0,DDU_IN) and T0-7's overlapping
''               testSetup(), which deliberately provoke a library abort; "aborted" there is
''               judged by a completion flag, never the trapped value. main() no longer traps each
''               testT0_n() (that nested a trap inside another trap's frame, PL-44 H7); exactly
''               ONE top-level trap now covers the whole run (\runTier0Tests()), and its value is
''               printed on every run, not only on abort. R1-T0-START, R1-T0-RESTART and
''               R3-T0-STOPPED gained a positive control: an independent testGetMotorCog()
''               readback that must agree with start()'s own return, so a stuck value cannot
''               satisfy the cell by accident.
''               14 Sep 2026 -- task 3542 (PL-42/PL-39): T0-12's panel now actually draws, following
''               the crop-and-overlay technique in DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/ and the
''               in-repo precedent in DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/debug_260912-153807.log
''               (test_bench_char.spin2's since-removed panel) -- LAYER/CROP/UPDATE against new
''               assets from tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py (t0h_bg.bmp/t0h_state.bmp/t0h_digits.bmp),
''               redrawn at the same ~500 ms cadence as the existing progress line so the 1 ms
''               hall poll is never slowed. Records the direction the operator was told
''               (T0_12_TOLD_CCW) and a signed tick position, decoded locally from a hand-copy of
''               isp_bldc_motor.spin2's deltas65 table, in the T0-12,started/running/end lines, for
''               PL-39. No sign-off cell is added or changed -- T0-12 declares none (confirmed
''               against DOCs/analyses/bench/SIGNOFF-MANIFEST.tsv, which carries no T0-12 row).
''               The told direction is fixed at CW (the panel bakes it in), and the delta read uses
''               SIGNX 7. The .bmp assets are generated by tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py and committed
''               beside this file.
''               15 Sep 2026 -- T0-12's panel names the wheel (RIGHT, the P16 board) and shows the
''               270-transition target; only S starts the count and only SPACE stops it, so a stray key
''               cannot end it (STEPHEN 2026-09-15: "a very careful working user interface"). Rendering
''               is shown only by the t0-hand run on the rig.
''               16 Sep 2026 -- task 3560 (Visit 4), SRC_REV 2: the 6.0.0 error contract, front cog and API
''               fixes arrive with cells. Nothing in the library aborts any more (tasks 3554/3555), so
''               T0-6 and T0-7 judge returned codes and the abort-probe traps and their completion flag
''               are deleted. T0-3 starts the motor first: a stop limit on an unstarted motor is now
''               refused with ERR_NOT_STARTED (F-5). R1-T0-RESTART expects 2 cogs per start (task 3513).
''               New cells T0-16..T0-22: R16-T0-BADGROUP, R16-T0-PINSKEEP (PL-48), R16-T0-LIMKEEP (F-4),
''               R16-T0-STRNOTSTART (F-5c), R16-T0-STEERCOGS, R16-T0-RESTZERO (PL-45),
''               R16-T0-NOBOARD (PL-25), R16-T0-FRONTFAIL. The banner prints src_rev.
''               17 Sep 2026 -- SRC_REV=3: this tier is now built with -D BENCH_QUIET (PL-74). No line
''               of this file changes behaviour; only the LIBRARY's debug channels are quieted, and this
''               binary judges RETURN CODES, not library chatter -- every cell below prints through a
''               plain debug() that no channel mask touches. WHY: at SRC_REV 2 this tier emitted NOTHING
''               on two separate runs, on two machines and two pnut-ts versions, from images that were
''               MEASURED to be debug builds (43_784 bytes with -d against 25_764 without). SRC_REV 2 is
''               also what added motorP and steer, taking this binary to SIX isp_bldc_motor instances
''               plus a steering object -- more than any other tier, and the only one compiled with the
''               library's nine channels live in all of them. MEASURED: -D BENCH_QUIET removes 2_866
''               bytes of library debug data from this build. THAT IS A HYPOTHESIS WITH A TEST, NOT AN
''               ESTABLISHED CAUSE; PL-74 records what the next run discriminates either way.
''               17 Sep 2026 -- task 3570, SRC_REV 4: T0-23 / R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART (PL-73): a start() on
''               the empty group is refused with ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED and leaks nothing.
''               18 Sep 2026 -- task 3517, SRC_REV 5: style guide 5.4.1 -- waitReady() is bWaitReady(). No
''               line changes.
''               18 Sep 2026 -- task 3543, SRC_REV 7 (PL-41, PL-85): the cog bursts that cut records at
''               Visit 5 are designed out. benchLog.countFreeCogs() counts with COGCHK() and starts nothing; T0-8,
''               T0-15b and T0-22 share one occupancy in runExhaustionPhase(), run last (T0-22 moves there,
''               a new T0-EXH line brackets the phase); every start()/stop() and spacer burst sits in a
''               benchLog cog-event quiet window. Every cell id, criterion and record format is unchanged.
''               19 Sep 2026 -- task 3577, SRC_REV 8: three cells for task 3569's API promises, which no
''               cell could certify. R17-T0-ACCEL (G): T0-5 becomes a cell -- setAcceleration() refuses a
''               rate outside its range and changes nothing, and an accepted rate is a constant mm/s^2 ramp
''               anchored on the library's own default. R17-T0-KMMI (K), in T0-3 on its running motor:
''               kilometres and miles convert exactly and can be commanded. R17-T0-VOLTGET (AK), in T0-19:
''               the drive voltage getter answers on both objects, and not before a start.
''               19 Sep 2026 -- task 3574, SRC_REV 9: prints for findings fixed in source are retired. T0-1
''               becomes R17-T0-DEADGAP (A1: the dead gap is at least 250 ns at this clock); T0-2 (A2/A3) and
''               T0-4 (O) are deleted, T0-4's testSetup() moving into T0-5; T0-10 drops its start_return
''               print (AD+). Cell R17-T0-DEADGAP is new; every other cell is unchanged.
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Rig: the dual 6.5" platform -- two Rev B boards, 18.5V pack.

  BUILD WITH -D BENCH_CFG. That selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2,
  a peer config file stating the bench and nothing else, in place of
  isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2. Nobody has to activate a block, and the
  file end users edit is neither read nor written by a bench run:

      pnut-ts -l -d -D BENCH_CFG test_bench_t0.spin2

  It still compiles without the flag -- build-check.sh does exactly that --
  against whichever user block is active. Under a block with
  WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH = 0.0 the T0-3 and T0-6 distance conversions correctly
  report themselves unavailable rather than returning a tick count.

  Every test below calls testSetup(), which runs the whole of init() -- board
  detection, constant derivation, power tables, unit conversion -- WITHOUT
  starting a driver cog, so the motor rail can stay off and the motor can stay
  unplugged. The exceptions are T0-10 (needs a real, running driver cog so the
  fourth ADC channel is actively calibrated and frame-locked; it still
  commands zero speed, so nothing turns), T0-11 (five real start()/stop()
  cycles reading live telemetry at zero command), T0-13 (a real start() held
  at zero command for 1000 ms), T0-14b (a real start()/stop() cycle to prove
  the post-stop board-type read stays clean), T0-15 (start()/stop() cycles
  probing cog accounting), T0-3 (a stop limit is accepted only by a started
  motor), and T0-17, T0-19, T0-20 and T0-22 (the 6.0.0 start, steering-start,
  rest-zero and front-cog-failure cells). Keep the motor rail on for all of
  these; none of them ever commands nonzero speed.

  Output: one tagged line per data point, "T0-n,field,value,...", on the plain
  debug stream. Sign-off records ("SIGNOFF-DECL,..." / "SIGNOFF,...") are a
  second, separately-tagged stream, read from the log into each visit's
  analysis report (design DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md).

  TRAPS (task 3539, PL-44/PL-47): a `\`-trap is an exceptional-return-path
  device, not a routine way to capture a normal result (STEPHEN: "traps are
  an exeptional return path - not normal use"). Since the 6.0.0 error contract
  (tasks 3554/3555) the library aborts nowhere: every command returns a status
  (0 or a negative ERR_*) and records it for getError(), and start()/startEx()
  return the cog id 0..7 or -1 with the cause in getError(). So every call below
  is UNTRAPPED and judged by its returned value and getError().

  ONE top-level trap covers the whole suite: main() calls `\runTier0Tests()`
  and prints its trapped value on EVERY run, so an abort nothing anticipated
  still shows up instead of silently ending the session. A testT0_n() that goes
  silent under such an abort skips its own SIGNOFF lines, and any declared cell
  with no verdict is NOMEAS by the host's convention (reason NOT_REACHED).

  T0-1's six derived constants (dead_gap, pwm_limit, duty_min, duty_max,
  adc_fram, frame_cnt) and T0-3 (finding F) both read via two new TEST-USE
  ONLY getters on isp_bldc_motor.spin2: testGetDriveConstants() and
  testGetStopHallTicks(). Both are pure read-only snapshots.

  Every start() here, the steering start included, commands zero speed, so
  nothing turns. If anything behaves unexpectedly: physical battery
  disconnect. emergencyCutoff() latches until clearEmergency() since task
  3556 (S-4 retired), but it is a software stop, not a panic button.

  T0-12 (hand-rotation anchor) is deliberately NOT part of this unattended
  run. It is compiled in only under -D T0_HAND, has its own bench-run.sh tier
  (t0-hand), waits on an operator keypress rather than a timer, and carries
  no sign-off cell.
}

CON { bench target }

' Which motor this harness talks to. Deliberately NOT read from the user
' config: a dual-motor block defines LEFT_MOTOR_BASE and RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE and
' no ONLY_MOTOR_BASE at all, so reading that user constant will not COMPILE on
' a dual bench -- which is what the real bench is (dual 6.5" wheels, Rev B
' boards, 18.5V pack). PINS_P16_P31 is a real motor under every config block
' in isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2: the right wheel on the dual 6.5"/18.5V
' block, the left wheel on the alternate dual block, and the sole motor on
' every single-motor block. Everything else -- motor type, drive voltage,
' wheel diameter -- still comes from whichever block is active, so the harness
' describes the hardware the operator says is connected.
    T0_MOTOR_BASE = motor.PINS_P16_P31

' Second populated base for T0-14's board-detection sweeps (R2-T0-REPEAT,
' R2-T0-DIRTY). PINS_P32_P47 is a legal enum value under every config block
' regardless of which is active, so this compiles everywhere; it is only
' actually wired to a second board on the dual-motor bench. Using the raw
' PINS_* enum (not user.LEFT_MOTOR_BASE) sidesteps the same single-motor
' compile hazard T0_MOTOR_BASE's comment above describes.
    T0_SECOND_BASE = motor.PINS_P32_P47

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV = 10                                              ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes; printed in the banner

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                      ' matches the audit's worked dead_gap example
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    READY_WAIT_MS  = 2_000                                      ' bound on a started driver reporting ready
    READY_POLL_MS  = 10

CON { 6.0.0 cells (task 3560) }

    BAD_PIN_BASE     = 99                                       ' not a PINS_* value: start() must reject it before any cog or pin is touched
    PL48_MARK_BASE   = 8                                        ' P8..P15: the release demo's HDMI group (PL-48)
    PL48_MARK_SPAN   = 7                                        ' addpins operand: 8 pins
    PL48_MARK_MASK   = $FF                                      ' DIRA bits 8..15, shifted down
    PL48_MARK_SHIFT  = 8
    SF_START_COGS    = 2                                        ' DERIVED -- task 3513: a single-motor start() is the driver plus its front cog
    SF_STEER_COGS    = 3                                        ' DERIVED -- task 3513: two owned drivers plus the steering front cog
    REST_SAMPLES     = 50                                       ' R16-T0-RESTZERO: getCurrent() reads averaged per board
    REST_SAMPLE_MS   = 20
    SF_REST_LO       = -100                                     ' DERIVED -- +/-10 mA (0.1 mA units); unfixed LEFT read ~535 (PL-45, Visit 1)
    SF_REST_HI       = 100

CON { API promise and regression cells (tasks 3577, 3574) }

' R17-T0-ACCEL: the library documents its built-in ramp as starting "near 44 mm/s squared", and that ramp's
'  start is the default ramp_min it reads back before any call. DERIVED: 1_500 steps x 0.02945 mm/s^2 per
'  step (1913 passes/s, 6 ticks per electrical cycle, 5.76 mm per tick, 2^32 per cycle) = 44.2 mm/s^2. So
'  setAcceleration(ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2) must land within 1% of the default ramp_min: a factor wrong anywhere
'  in the conversion moves it far outside that.
    ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2 = 44
    ACCEL_ANCHOR_TOL_DIV = 100                                  ' 1% of the default ramp_min
    ACCEL_BELOW_RANGE  = -1                                     ' a negative rate, as well as the one just below range
' R17-T0-KMMI: exact unit identities the conversion must reproduce tick for tick
    M_PER_KM           = 1_000
    FT_PER_MI          = 5_280
' R17-T0-VOLTGET: the bench pack's nominal voltage (the bench config's PWR_18p5V, the 5S pack -- STEPHEN
'  2026-09-17, "18.5 V nominal 5S"). The harness is built with -D BENCH_CFG, so that is the voltage start() gets.
    SF_PACK_MV         = 18_500
' R17-T0-DEADGAP (task 3574, A1 / PL-9): both 64010 manuals' minimum commutation dead gap, either board
    DEADTIME_MIN_NS    = 250
    HZ_PER_MHZ         = 1_000_000
    NS_PER_US          = 1_000
' each cell's n: the claims its one verdict covers
    DEADGAP_READS_JUDGED = 1
    ACCEL_CALLS_JUDGED = 5                                      ' three refusals, the anchor, the top rate
    KMMI_CLAIMS_JUDGED = 3                                      ' km conversion, mi conversion, the refusal
    VOLT_READS_JUDGED  = 3                                      ' motor, steering running, steering not started

CON { cog-exhaustion probe (T0-8, T0-15) }

    MAX_SPACER_COGS   = 7                                       ' every cog besides this harness's own
    SPACER_STACK_LONGS = 32                                     ' generous headroom for a trivial idle loop

CON { hand-rotation anchor (T0-12, -D T0_HAND only) }

    T0_12_HALL_OFFSET = 5                                       ' pin_hall_u is base+5; hall inputs are base+5..base+7
    T0_12_HALL_SPAN   = 2                                       ' addpins operand: three hall pins
    T0_12_POLL_MS     = 1                                       ' hall poll period while counting
    T0_12_KEY_POLLS   = 100                                     ' polls between keypress checks (~100 ms) -- matches
                                                                 ' PC_KEY's own ~100 ms keypress-latch window
                                                                 ' (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7)
    T0_12_PRINT_POLLS = 500                                     ' polls between progress lines AND panel redraws
                                                                 ' (~500 ms); the panel rides this existing cadence
                                                                 ' rather than adding a new one, so it costs nothing
                                                                 ' extra against the 1 ms hall poll (PL-42 fix)
    T0_12_KEY_WAIT_MS = 50                                      ' keypress poll period before counting starts
    T0_12_KEY_START   = "S"                                     ' starts the count (either case); no other key does
    T0_12_KEY_START_LC = "s"
    T0_12_KEY_STOP    = " "                                     ' SPACE stops the count; no other key does
    T0_12_REVOLUTIONS = 3                                       ' operator turns exactly this many full revolutions;
                                                                 ' baked into t0h_bg.bmp -- regenerate that asset
                                                                 ' (tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py) if this changes

' PL-39: the direction the operator is TOLD to turn, viewed from the hub side, is fixed at CW. The
' panel background bakes the instruction in (tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py), so a second direction
' would need a second asset set that could disagree with the log; instead one known direction plus
' the signed tick change (pos) is enough to tie the tick sign to the physical direction.
    T0_12_TOLD_CCW    = FALSE

CON { T0-12 panel geometry -- GENERATED by tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py, do not hand-edit }

    T0H_PANEL_W       = 420
    T0H_PANEL_H       = 240
    T0H_PANEL_POS_X   = 60
    T0H_PANEL_POS_Y   = 80

    T0H_LYR_BG        = 1
    T0H_LYR_STATE     = 2
    T0H_LYR_DGT       = 3

    T0H_STATE_X       = 12
    T0H_STATE_Y       = 104
    T0H_STATE_W       = 200
    T0H_STATE_H       = 32
    T0H_STATE_WAITING = 0
    T0H_STATE_COUNTING = 1
    T0H_STATE_DONE    = 2

    T0H_DGT_W         = 32
    T0H_DGT_H         = 40
    T0H_DGT_BLANK     = 10                                      ' cell 10 in t0h_digits.bmp is blank

    T0H_TRANS_X       = 140
    T0H_TRANS_Y       = 140
    T0H_TRANS_PITCH   = 34
    T0H_TRANS_COUNT   = 4                                       ' up to 9999 transitions

    T0H_ILL_X         = 140
    T0H_ILL_Y         = 184
    T0H_ILL_PITCH     = 34
    T0H_ILL_COUNT     = 3                                       ' up to 999 illegal-code entries

CON { T0-24 panel geometry -- GENERATED by tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py, do not hand-edit }

' The T0S_LYR_* numbers below RECORD which layer holds which artwork; they cannot be referenced
' from the code, because a DEBUG backtick command takes the window name and the layer as literal
' tokens rather than expressions. Changing one here moves nothing -- change the literal in
' t0sSetupPanel()/t0sDrawPanel() and this number together.

    T0S_PANEL_W       = 480
    T0S_PANEL_H       = 300
    T0S_PANEL_POS_X   = 60
    T0S_PANEL_POS_Y   = 80

    T0S_LYR_BG        = 1
    T0S_LYR_ROW       = 2
    T0S_LYR_ACT       = 3
    T0S_LYR_DGT       = 4

    T0S_ROW_X         = 12
    T0S_ROW_Y         = 36
    T0S_ROW_W         = 456
    T0S_ROW_H         = 28

    T0S_ACT_X         = 12
    T0S_ACT_Y         = 70
    T0S_ACT_W         = 456
    T0S_ACT_H         = 64

    T0S_DGT_W         = 28
    T0S_DGT_H         = 36
    T0S_DGT_BLANK     = 10

    T0S_READ_X        = 170
    T0S_READ_PITCH    = 30
    T0S_HAND_Y        = 146
    T0S_AFTER_Y       = 190
    T0S_MS_Y          = 234
    T0S_HAND_COUNT    = 4
    T0S_AFTER_COUNT   = 4
    T0S_MS_COUNT      = 5

CON { stop-state hand test (T0-24, -D T0_STOPMODE only) }

' Six rows, one wheel. Each row puts the driver in exactly ONE stop state and then measures how
' that state answers a hand on the wheel. The panel names what Stephen does BEFORE each row runs
' (overlay P1), and his key press only sequences the row: every verdict below is an instrument
' reading, never his opinion (overlay P7). The predictions are DOCs/plans/STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS5.
    T0_24_ROW_COUNT     = 6
    T0_24_ROW_HOLD      = 0                                     ' holdAtStop(TRUE) at rest: the powered hold (BR_DRIVE)
    T0_24_ROW_COAST     = 1                                     ' holdAtStop(FALSE) at rest: BR_COAST
    T0_24_ROW_ESTOP     = 2                                     ' emergencyCutoff(): BR_SHORT
    T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST  = 3                                     ' a provoked fault under SM_FLOAT: BR_COAST
    T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD   = 4                                     ' a provoked fault under SM_BRAKE: BR_SHORT
    T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP   = 5                                     ' stop(): the pins released -- the free yardstick, LAST

' The action cell each phase shows, indexing t0s_actions.bmp (tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py)
    T0_24_ACT_ARM       = 0
    T0_24_ACT_SETUP     = 1
    T0_24_ACT_POWERED   = 2
    T0_24_ACT_TURNSLOW  = 3
    T0_24_ACT_SPIN      = 4
    T0_24_ACT_COASTING  = 5
    T0_24_ACT_ROWDONE   = 6
    T0_24_ACT_ALLDONE   = 7
    T0_24_ROW_ALLDONE   = T0_24_ROW_COUNT                       ' the row layer's cell after the six, shown once they are done

    T0_24_POLL_MS       = 1                                     ' hall poll period, as T0-12 polls (5 revolutions per second
                                                                 ' before two transitions could fall between polls)
    T0_24_KEY_POLLS     = 100                                   ' polls between keypress checks (~100 ms), matching PC_KEY's
                                                                 ' own latch window (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7)
    T0_24_PRINT_POLLS   = 500                                   ' polls between panel redraws (~500 ms), as T0-12 redraws
    T0_24_KEY_WAIT_MS   = 50                                    ' keypress poll period while waiting to arm a row
    T0_24_KEY_SAMPLES   = 20                                    ' T0_24_SAMPLE_MS samples between keypress checks inside a
                                                                 ' powered window: 20 x 5 ms is the same ~100 ms cadence
    T0_24_KEY_START     = "S"                                   ' arms the next row (either case); no other key does
    T0_24_KEY_START_LC  = "s"
    T0_24_KEY_STOP      = " "                                   ' SPACE ends the hand phase, and aborts a powered row
    T0_24_HAND_CAP_MS   = 120_000                               ' bound on the hand phase: a row nobody ends still ends
    T0_24_COAST_CAP_MS  = 20_000                                ' bound on the after-release phase
    T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS = 400                                   ' no hall transition for this long = the wheel is at rest
    T0_24_TICK_RING     = 6                                     ' tick timestamps kept: one electrical cycle of hall ticks,
                                                                 ' so the rate reading spans a whole commutation cycle and
                                                                 ' cogging cannot bias one tick's interval
    T0_24_HALF_FACTOR   = 2                                     ' "half the release rate" = twice the release interval

' The provoked fault (rows 4 and 5) is R17.5's COMPUTED provocation, ported to one wheel: drive to
' speed, read this wheel's own position error, and shift both commutation offsets by exactly what
' moves that error onto the driver's fault test. Same power as the dual harness's own provocation,
' so this tier's post-fault readings and R17-DUAL-FLTSTOP-C's compare.
    T0_24_FLT_POWER     = 50                                    ' driveAtPower(50), the dual harness's FLTAPI_POWER
    T0_24_SPEED_MS      = 4_000                                 ' AT_SPEED bound (the dual harness's STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
    T0_24_SETTLE_MS     = 1_000                                 ' at speed before the error reads
    T0_24_SAMPLE_MS     = 5                                     ' poll cadence of every bounded wait here
    T0_24_ERR_SAMPLES   = 16                                    ' err reads averaged at speed before the shift
    T0_24_NO_FAULT_MS   = 2_000                                 ' wait for the provoked fault; none by then is NO_FAULT
    T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED   = 0                                     ' the two driver states a powered window ever waits on
    T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT   = 1
    T0_24_REST_WAIT_MS  = 30_000                                ' bound on the post-fault coast to rest
    T0_24_ERR_PER_TURN  = 256                                   ' the driver's err: one electrical cycle, signed 8-bit
    T0_24_ERR_MASK      = T0_24_ERR_PER_TURN - 1
    T0_24_ERR_TARGET    = 128                                   ' = -128: the wrap point, 3 units past the |err| >= 125 test
    T0_24_DEG_PER_TURN  = 360
    T0_24_ABORT_AMPS    = 100_000                               ' 10 A in getCurrent()'s 0.1 mA units: the powered window's
                                                                 ' absolute abort, the same ceiling the dual harness aborts on

CON { T0-24 sign-off limits -- each with its provenance }

' The discriminating reading is NOT how far the wheel carries on: that scales with however hard
' Stephen pushed. It is how long the wheel takes to fall to HALF the rate it had when he let go.
' A shorted winding brakes with a torque proportional to speed, so that time is a property of the
' bridge state and not of his push; a free wheel decays on bearing and cogging drag alone.
' DERIVED from PL-56's Visit 2 measurement (STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS2): emergencyCutoff() -- the
' SHORT state -- stopped a half-speed wheel within ONE tick, where stop() coasted 38-48 ticks.
' At a hand's rate that puts SHORT's half-rate time at a few tick intervals (tens of ms) and a
' free wheel's at a few hundred; the two limits below leave a 90 ms dead band between them, so
' neither verdict can be reached by the other state's reading.
    SF_FREE_HALF_MS     = 150                                   ' DERIVED -- at or above this, the wheel is freewheeling
    SF_BRAKE_HALF_MS    = 60                                    ' DERIVED -- at or below this, the wheel is being braked
    SF_MODE_GAP_MS      = 100                                   ' DERIVED -- the gap two stop modes must differ by, the shape
                                                                 ' of the dual harness's own FLTSTOP_GAP_TICKS
    SF_HAND_MIN_TICKS   = 10                                    ' DERIVED -- the row is judged only when the wheel actually
                                                                 ' moved: 10 hall ticks is 40 degrees of wheel, and the tick
                                                                 ' ring needs its six before a release rate exists

DAT { owning task numbers, printed in each cell's records }

sTaskPromises   BYTE    "3577", 0                               ' the API-promise cells: ACCEL, KMMI, VOLTGET
sTaskCleanup    BYTE    "3574", 0                               ' the bench-cleanup cell: DEADGAP
sTaskStopMode   BYTE    "3578", 0                               ' the stop-state hand-test cells (T0-24)

sCellHoldPwr    BYTE    "R17-T0-HOLDPWR", 0                     ' row 1: the hold at rest is powered
sCellRestCoast  BYTE    "R17-T0-RESTCOAST", 0                   ' row 2: holdAtStop(FALSE) at rest really coasts
sCellRestShort  BYTE    "R17-T0-RESTSHORT", 0                   ' row 3: the e-stop brakes -- and so did the old float
sCellStopGap    BYTE    "R17-T0-STOPGAP", 0                     ' rows 2 and 3 are different states, by a margin
sCellFltCoast   BYTE    "R17-T0-FLTCOAST", 0                    ' row 4: a fault under SM_FLOAT coasts
sCellFltShort   BYTE    "R17-T0-FLTSHORT", 0                    ' row 5: a fault under SM_BRAKE brakes
sCellFltGap     BYTE    "R17-T0-FLTGAP", 0                      ' rows 4 and 5 are different states, by a margin
sCellFreeRef    BYTE    "R17-T0-FREEREF", 0                     ' row 6: the released pins, this run's free yardstick

sCritHoldPwr    BYTE    "TURN_RECORDS_FAULT", 0
sCritRestCoast  BYTE    "COAST_HALF_MS", 0
sCritRestShort  BYTE    "SHORT_HALF_MS", 0
sCritStopGap    BYTE    "COAST_LESS_SHORT_MS", 0
sCritFltCoast   BYTE    "FLT_COAST_HALF_AND_FAULTED", 0
sCritFltShort   BYTE    "FLT_SHORT_HALF_AND_FAULTED", 0
sCritFltGap     BYTE    "FLTCOAST_LESS_FLTHOLD_MS", 0
sCritFreeRef    BYTE    "FREE_HALF_MS", 0

DAT { T0-12 hand-copy of the driver's hall-position-delta table (PL-39) }

' HAND-MAINTAINED COPY of isp_bldc_motor.spin2:1885-1892 (deltas65), indexed (old<<3 | new) same as
' the driver's own pos_ accumulation (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2490-2497, "altgb hall_, #deltas /
' getbyte / signx tmpY, #7 / add pos_, tmpY"). This file starts no driver cog, so it decodes the
' sign of the hand turn itself rather than reading the driver's pos. If the library's deltas65
' table ever changes, this copy drifts silently -- there is no shared symbol between a Spin2 DAT
' array here and the PASM DAT the driver copies into its cog image. Read with `SIGNX 7`, matching
' the driver's own `signx tmpY, #7`, since a Spin2 BYTE array read is unsigned 0..255 (Spin2's `~`
' is post-clear, not a sign extend -- p2kbSpin2Operators).

t0hHallDeltas65    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0,-1, 0, 1, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0,-1, 0
                    BYTE    0, 1,-1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 0, 0,-1, 1, 0
                    BYTE    0,-1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 1, 0,-1, 0, 0, 0
                    BYTE    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

CON { sign-off limits (task 3504) -- compiled-in CON limits per cell, each with its provenance;
      full derivations in DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS A.4/A.5 }

    SF_ZXS_LO     = 0            ' definitional -- a max - min spread cannot be negative
    SF_ZXS_HI     = 50           ' DERIVED -- SS A.5-e: 2x the predicted post-fix spread (~2.5 mV), in MV_X10

    SF_STOP_LO    = 0
    SF_STOP_HI    = 0            ' DERIVED -- stationary halls never transition (SS A.4 row 3)

    SF_REPEAT_LO  = 0
    SF_REPEAT_HI  = 0            ' DERIVED -- every one of 32 reads on a real board must read REV_B

    SF_TICKS_LO   = 173
    SF_TICKS_HI   = 174          ' DERIVED -- SS A.5-b: 1000 mm x 90 / 518.6 mm = 173.5, truncated or rounded

    SF_COG_LO     = 0
    SF_COG_HI     = 7            ' DERIVED -- start() returns a cog id 0..7 on success (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:86)

    SF_RESTART_LO = 0            ' DERIVED -- PL-24 fix: a second start() must orphan no cog; each start() now costs SF_START_COGS

    SF_EXHAUST_LO = -1           ' DERIVED -- start()'s own -1-on-failure contract (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:86, :121); coginit()'s
                                 ' own observed exhaustion form is $8000_xxxx (:110-112), not -1 -- corrected per PL-44 finding 7

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"                 ' bench compile-time hardware config (-D BENCH_CFG)
#else
    user    : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"                       ' active compile-time hardware config
#endif
    motor   : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' primary instance, T0-1/3/5/6/8/10/11/13/14/15
    motorA  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' second instance, T0-7 overlap probe, T0-14b scratch, T0-16/T0-21/T0-22
    motorB  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' second instance, T0-7 overlap probe only
    motorP  : "isp_bldc_motor"                                  ' T0-17 (PL-48) only: an instance nothing else has touched
    steer   : "isp_steering_2wheel"                             ' T0-18 (never started first) and T0-19 (cog count, R17-T0-VOLTGET)
    benchLog : "isp_bench_log"                                  ' the cog-event quiet window (PL-41, PL-85)

VAR { cog-exhaustion spacer stacks (runExhaustionPhase(): T0-8, T0-15b, T0-22) }

    LONG    spacerStacks[MAX_SPACER_COGS * SPACER_STACK_LONGS]
    LONG    heldSpacerId[MAX_SPACER_COGS]                       ' occupySpacers() / releaseSpacers(): the spacers held across a start

VAR { run state }

' R16-T0-NOABORT: T0-6's two returned codes, judged together with T0-7's in one cell
    LONG    bUnitsCodesOk

' R10-T0-STOPREADY (T0-15d) judges the state T0-15c's own stop() left behind, so it is valid
' only when T0-15c ran to that stop() with both start()s returning a real cog id (0..7). A
' start() that returns -1 also calls stop() (the PL-36 failure branch), which leaves DCS_Unknown
' with no driver ever run -- a PASS read from nothing. T0-15c clears this first and sets it last.
    LONG    bRestartStopValid

' R17-T0-VOLTGET (judged in T0-19, beside the steering object's own reads) compares against the motor object's
' getDriveVoltage(), read by T0-3 while its motor runs. T0-3 clears the flag first and sets it once the read is taken.
    LONG    motorVolt
    LONG    motorMilliVolts
    LONG    bMotorVoltRead

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
VAR { T0-24 per-row readings (-D T0_STOPMODE only) }

' One row's readings, kept per row because three cells compare two rows with each other. Only
' this build declares them, so the unattended t0 binary carries none of it.
    LONG    t0sHandTicks[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                       ' hall ticks while his hand was on the wheel
    LONG    t0sAfterTicks[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                      ' hall ticks after he let go
    LONG    t0sAfterMs[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                         ' how long those took
    LONG    t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                          ' ms from the release to half the release rate: the criterion
    LONG    bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                    ' TRUE when the row's state was reached AND he turned the wheel
    LONG    bT0sStillFaulted[T0_24_ROW_COUNT]                   ' rows 4 and 5: the driver was still FAULTED when the row ended
    LONG    bT0sHoldFaulted                                     ' row 1: the driver recorded a fault while he turned the hold
#endif

PUB main() | trapCode
'' Run every Tier 0 test in sequence and tag its result on the debug stream. Exactly ONE
'' top-level trap covers the whole run (task 3539, PL-44/PL-47): main() calls \runTier0Tests()
'' and prints trapCode on EVERY run, not only when something aborted (P3), so a genuine abort
'' this file did not anticipate is visible instead of silently ending the session. Individual
'' tests are no longer separately \-trapped -- that was a trap nested inside this one's frame,
'' PL-44's H7 suspect -- and normal library calls inside them are made untrapped and judged by
'' their returned value. The very last thing printed, alone on its own line with nothing else in
'' that debug() call, is the literal text DEBUG_END_SESSION -- tools/bench-run.sh runs
'' pnut-term-ts with --exit-on-end-session, and that phrase is its end-of-session marker.
'' Emitting it here, only after DONE, lets that batch mode close the terminal itself once the
'' suite has genuinely finished, instead of waiting on an operator keypress or a fixed timeout.
'' No other debug() output anywhere in this harness may contain this phrase, or the session
'' would end early.
''

' @local trapCode - the top-level trap's value: 0 on a normal return from runTier0Tests()
'                    (it returns nothing meaningful), or the abort value if something aborted

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
    ' T0-24 is the one build of this harness that drives the motor: rows 4 and 5 provoke a fault at
    '  T0_24_FLT_POWER. The banner says so, because "no motion" in a log this build wrote would be
    '  a false description of what the operator was standing next to.
    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- T0-24 stop-state hand test: ATTENDED, THE WHEEL SPINS ON TWO ROWS -- src_rev ", udec_(SRC_REV))
#else
    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- Tier 0: no motion -- src_rev ", udec_(SRC_REV))
#endif
    debug("* active config: motor_type_enum=", udec_(user.MOTOR_TYPE), " base=", udec_(T0_MOTOR_BASE), " voltage_enum=", udec_(user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE), " wheel_dia_x10=", udec_(round(user.WHEEL_DIA_IN_INCH *. 10.0)))
    debug("* bench expects MOTOR_TYPE=MOTR_6_5_INCH (0) and wheel_dia_x10=65; with wheel_dia_x10=0 the T0-3/T0-6 distance conversions report unavailable rather than a tick count")

    trapCode := \runTier0Tests()
    debug("T0-TRAP,code,", sdec_(trapCode))                  ' P3: printed every run, not only on abort

    debug("* test_bench_t0 -- DONE")
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")

PRI runTier0Tests()
' The single top-level trap's body (called only as \runTier0Tests() from main()). No call in
' here is itself \-trapped except T0-6's and T0-7's own deliberate abort probes -- see their
' comments -- so this is the only trap frame any of them can nest inside.
'

#ifdef T0_HAND
    ' T0_HAND build (bench-run.sh t0-hand): T0-12 only. It is an operator-attended reference
    ' measurement with no sign-off cell, so this build runs none of the unattended tests and
    ' declares no cells -- its log can never be mistaken for an unattended Tier 0 run.
    testT0_12()
#elseifdef T0_STOPMODE
    ' T0_STOPMODE build (bench-run.sh t0-stopmode): T0-24 only, for the same reason -- it waits on
    ' a person at every row, and on two rows it drives the motor. Its cells are its own.
    testT0_24()
#else
    ' Sign-off declarations (design rule 3, SS 0): one per cell this binary will judge, emitted
    ' before anything starts a cog. Row 8 (R8-T0-ZXS) covers all four channel variants (ZXS_I/
    ' U/V/W) under a single declared cell, per design SS A.2's "feature row is the set of cells
    ' sharing row" -- the manifest joins on the cell id, not the per-channel crit token.
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-REPEAT,task,3500")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-DIRTY,task,3500")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-EMPTY,task,3500")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R4-T0-1M-TICKS,task,3502")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-START,task,3499")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-RESTART,task,3499")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R10-T0-STOPREADY,task,3533")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-EXHAUST,task,3499")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-LIMKEEP,task,3554")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-NOABORT,task,3554")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-BADGROUP,task,3554")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-PINSKEEP,task,3554")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-STRNOTSTART,task,3555")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-STEERCOGS,task,3513")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-RESTZERO,task,3556")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-NOBOARD,task,3556")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-FRONTFAIL,task,3513")
    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART,task,3570")
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-DEADGAP", @sTaskCleanup)
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-ACCEL", @sTaskPromises)
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-KMMI", @sTaskPromises)
    emitCellDecl(@"R17-T0-VOLTGET", @sTaskPromises)

    testT0_1()
    testT0_3()
    testT0_5()
    testT0_6()
    testT0_7()

    ' T0-18 before anything starts the steering object: it judges a never-started instance
    testT0_18()

    ' T0-11 and T0-13 run BEFORE T0-10 (design SS H.1 order rule): both are real start()/stop()
    ' cycles on `motor`, and running them before T0-10's own start()/stop() (and well before
    ' T0-8's destructive cog exhaustion) keeps every one of their five/one start()s clean.
    testT0_11()
    testT0_13()

    ' T0-14 (board-detection sweeps) also belongs on the non-destructive side of T0-8, and after
    ' T0-7 so it can release T0-7's motorA/motorB pin claims itself (each sub-test does so).
    testT0_14a()
    testT0_14b()
    testT0_14c()

    ' T0-15a/c/d (start/restart/stopready) are non-destructive cog accounting; T0-15b
    ' (exhaustion) is deliberately last, after T0-8's slot (see T0-8's own comment).
    testT0_15a()
    testT0_15c()
    testT0_15d()

    ' T0-16..T0-23 (task 3560): the 6.0.0 start, pin, steering, current-sense and no-board cells. Each
    ' releases every claim and cog it takes. T0-22 (front-cog failure) runs in the exhaustion phase below.
    testT0_16()
    testT0_17()
    testT0_19()
    testT0_20()
    testT0_21()
    testT0_23()

    ' T0-10 runs BEFORE the exhaustion phase deliberately. Both drive the same motor object,
    ' and the phase is destructive: it occupies every spare cog so that start() must fail,
    ' which leaves the object half-initialised. Run in the other order, T0-10's own start()
    ' then returns 0 and its ADC reading is never taken -- observed in the 2026-09-10 bench
    ' run. Destructive tests go last.
    testT0_10()

    ' The cog-exhaustion cells T0-8, R1-T0-EXHAUST (T0-15b, design SS H.1: never leaves fewer free
    ' cogs than it found) and R16-T0-FRONTFAIL (T0-22) run last, sharing ONE occupancy (PL-85).
    runExhaustionPhase()
#endif

PRI testT0_1() | deadGap, minGap, bPass
' A1 / R17-T0-DEADGAP (task 3574): the whole of init() runs through testSetup() and the commutation dead gap it
' derives is at least DEADTIME_MIN_NS at this clock. Both Parallax 64010 manuals specify a 250 ns minimum on
' either board revision (A1, PL-9); the library now uses 260 ns everywhere. UNFIXED: Rev B got 52 ns -- 14
' ticks at 270 MHz against the 68 this requires -- so the cell FAILs. testSetup() is called UNTRAPPED (task
' 3539): a genuine abort from a bad voltage/motor pairing is caught by main()'s single top-level trap. The
' values T0-1 used to print beside it (the other drive constants, the sense resistor, the board string) fed no
' cell and no open finding, so they are retired (task 3574).
'
' @local deadGap - dead_gap from testGetDriveConstants(), in system ticks
' @local minGap - the fewest ticks that are DEADTIME_MIN_NS at CLKFREQ, rounded up
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    deadGap, _, _, _, _, _ := motor.testGetDriveConstants()
    ' ticks per us x ns / 1000, rounded up. CLKFREQ / HZ_PER_MHZ truncates on a clock that is not a whole
    ' number of MHz; every clock this file is built at is (270 MHz here, 200/270/300 on the clock loads).
    minGap := ((CLKFREQ / HZ_PER_MHZ) * DEADTIME_MIN_NS + NS_PER_US - 1) / NS_PER_US
    bPass := (deadGap >= minGap)
    debug("T0-1,dead_gap,", udec_(deadGap), ",min_ticks,", udec_(minGap), ",clkfreq,", udec_(CLKFREQ))
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-DEADGAP", @sTaskCleanup, @"RIGHT", @"DEADTIME_250NS_MIN", TRUE, bPass, DEADGAP_READS_JUDGED)

PRI testT0_3() | startResult, bReady, eM, eCm, eMm, ticksM, ticksCm, ticksMm, bAgree, bTicksInBand, bPass, eRot, keptRot, eDist, keptDist, eTime, keptTime, bKeep, bKmMiOk
' F: stopAfterDistance() computes its tick target in three equivalent ways --
' 1 DDU_M, 100 DDU_CM, 1000 DDU_MM -- and stores it in the private VAR
' motorStopHallTicks, read back here via the testGetStopHallTicks() getter.
' All three should agree; DDU_M coming out a factor of ten short of the other
' two CONFIRMS finding F. Since the error contract (task 3554, F-5) a stop
' limit is accepted only by a started motor -- an unstarted one returns
' ERR_NOT_STARTED and arms nothing -- so the motor is started at zero command
' first. The limit is armed at rest and never crossed, so nothing turns.
'
' task 3504 / R4-T0-1M-TICKS: a BOOL cell (task 3537). measured is TRUE only when
' every call returned NO_ERROR, the DDU_M reading (ticksM) is in SF_TICKS_LO..
' SF_TICKS_HI (SS A.5-b) AND the three units agree.
'
' task 3554 / R16-T0-LIMKEEP (F-4): with the 1000 mm limit armed, three rejected
' calls -- stopAfterRotation(1, 99), stopAfterDistance(1, 99), stopAfterTime(0,
' DTU_SEC) -- must each return their code (ERR_BAD_UNITS, ERR_BAD_UNITS,
' ERR_BAD_COUNT) and leave the armed limit as it was. UNFIXED: stopAfterRotation()
' zeroed the armed limit before validating, and an illegal unit aborted.
'
' task 3577 / R17-T0-KMMI (K), on the same running motor after LIMKEEP: see bUnitsKmMiOk().
' The motor's getDriveVoltage() is read here too, for T0-19's R17-T0-VOLTGET.
' All three cells are NOMEAS when the start did not reach ready.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reported ready within READY_WAIT_MS
' @local eM - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)'s status
' @local eCm - stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM)'s status
' @local eMm - stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM)'s status
' @local ticksM - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)
' @local ticksCm - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(100, DDU_CM)
' @local ticksMm - motorStopHallTicks after stopAfterDistance(1000, DDU_MM)
' @local bAgree - TRUE when all three tick readings match (PL-23: printed as TRUE/FALSE)
' @local bTicksInBand - TRUE when ticksM falls in SF_TICKS_LO..SF_TICKS_HI
' @local bPass - R4-T0-1M-TICKS's measured value and verdict
' @local eRot - stopAfterRotation(1, 99)'s status
' @local keptRot - the armed limit after it
' @local eDist - stopAfterDistance(1, 99)'s status
' @local keptDist - the armed limit after it
' @local eTime - stopAfterTime(0, DTU_SEC)'s status
' @local keptTime - the armed limit after it
' @local bKeep - R16-T0-LIMKEEP's measured value and verdict
' @local bKmMiOk - R17-T0-KMMI's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-3,begin")
    bMotorVoltRead := FALSE
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    bReady := bWaitReady(startResult)
    debug("T0-3,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    if bReady
        eM := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, motor.DDU_M)
        ticksM := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        debug("T0-3,ddu_m,1,status,", sdec_(eM), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksM))

        eCm := motor.stopAfterDistance(100, motor.DDU_CM)
        ticksCm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        debug("T0-3,ddu_cm,100,status,", sdec_(eCm), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksCm))

        eMm := motor.stopAfterDistance(1000, motor.DDU_MM)
        ticksMm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        debug("T0-3,ddu_mm,1000,status,", sdec_(eMm), ",ticks,", udec_(ticksMm))

        bAgree := (ticksM == ticksCm) and (ticksCm == ticksMm)
        debug("T0-3,end,agree,", zstr_(bAgree ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

        bTicksInBand := (ticksM >= SF_TICKS_LO) and (ticksM <= SF_TICKS_HI)
        bPass := bAgree and bTicksInBand and (eM == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eCm == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eMm == motor.NO_ERROR)
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R4-T0-1M-TICKS,task,3502,motor,NONE,crit,DDU_M_TICKS,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

        eRot := motor.stopAfterRotation(1, 99)
        keptRot := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        eDist := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, 99)
        keptDist := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        eTime := motor.stopAfterTime(0, motor.DTU_SEC)
        keptTime := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
        bKeep := (eRot == motor.ERR_BAD_UNITS) and (eDist == motor.ERR_BAD_UNITS) and (eTime == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT)
        bKeep := bKeep and (ticksMm <> 0) and (keptRot == ticksMm) and (keptDist == ticksMm) and (keptTime == ticksMm)
        debug("T0-3,limkeep,armed,", udec_(ticksMm), ",rot_status,", sdec_(eRot), ",kept,", udec_(keptRot), ",dist_status,", sdec_(eDist), ",kept,", udec_(keptDist), ",time_status,", sdec_(eTime), ",kept,", udec_(keptTime))
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-LIMKEEP,task,3554,motor,RIGHT,crit,REJECT_KEEPS_LIMIT,measured,", zstr_(bKeep ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,3,verdict,", zstr_(bKeep ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

        bKmMiOk := bUnitsKmMiOk()
        emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-KMMI", @sTaskPromises, @"RIGHT", @"KM_MI_EXACT_CMD", TRUE, bKmMiOk, KMMI_CLAIMS_JUDGED)
        motorVolt, motorMilliVolts := motor.getDriveVoltage()
        bMotorVoltRead := TRUE
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R4-T0-1M-TICKS,task,3502,motor,NONE,crit,DDU_M_TICKS,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-LIMKEEP,task,3554,motor,RIGHT,crit,REJECT_KEEPS_LIMIT,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
        emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-KMMI", @sTaskPromises, @"RIGHT", @"KM_MI_EXACT_CMD", FALSE, FALSE, KMMI_CLAIMS_JUDGED)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motor.getError()                                        ' drain this cog's first recorded code, so a later cell reads only its own

PRI bWaitReady(startResult) : bReady | readyMs
' Wait, bounded by READY_WAIT_MS, for `motor` to report ready after a start() that returned a cog id.
'
' @param startResult - the start()'s return; a failed start (< 0) is never ready
' @returns bReady - TRUE when start() returned a cog id and the driver reported ready in the bound
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator

    bReady := FALSE
    if startResult >= 0
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < READY_WAIT_MS)
            waitms(READY_POLL_MS)
            readyMs += READY_POLL_MS
        bReady := motor.isReady()

PRI testT0_5() | minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef, eBelow, eNegative, eAbove, bRefuseOk, eAnchor, stepAnchor, bAnchorOk, eTop, stepTop, bTopOk, eRestore, bPass
' G / R17-T0-ACCEL (task 3577): setAcceleration() takes a rate in mm/s^2 at the rim, refuses one outside
' [ACCEL_MIN_MM_S2 .. ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2] with ERR_BAD_COUNT and changes nothing, and turns an accepted one into a
' constant ramp -- ramp_min == ramp_max == the step for that rate, ramp_inc 0, ramp_down untouched. The step for
' ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2 must land within 1% of the default ramp_min (see the constant's derivation), and a larger
' rate must give a larger step. Nothing starts: the test calls testSetup() itself for the wheel geometry.
' UNFIXED: {rate} went straight into ramp_inc with no check, so every refused rate changed the ramp and an
' accepted one left ramp_min and ramp_max at their defaults -- the cell FAILs on both halves.
' NOMEAS when the active config has no wheel diameter (ERR_NO_WHEEL_DIA): there is no rim to convert at.
'
' @local minDef - the default ramp_min, read back before any call
' @local maxDef - the default ramp_max
' @local incDef - the default ramp_inc
' @local decrDef - the default ramp_down
' @local eBelow - setAcceleration(ACCEL_MIN_MM_S2 - 1)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eNegative - setAcceleration(ACCEL_BELOW_RANGE)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eAbove - setAcceleration(ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2 + 1)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local bRefuseOk - every refusal returned its code and left the ramp as it was
' @local eAnchor - setAcceleration(ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2)'s return
' @local stepAnchor - the step it produced
' @local bAnchorOk - the anchor call produced a constant ramp within 1% of the default ramp_min
' @local eTop - setAcceleration(ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2)'s return
' @local stepTop - the step it produced
' @local bTopOk - the top rate produced a constant ramp with a larger step than the anchor's
' @local eRestore - setRampingValues()'s return restoring the defaults
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-5,begin")
    motor.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    motor.getError()                                        ' start from a clear slot
    minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef := motor.getRampingValues()

    eBelow := motor.setAcceleration(motor.ACCEL_MIN_MM_S2 - 1)
    bRefuseOk := (eBelow == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and bRampEquals(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)
    eNegative := motor.setAcceleration(ACCEL_BELOW_RANGE)
    bRefuseOk := bRefuseOk and (eNegative == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and bRampEquals(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)
    eAbove := motor.setAcceleration(motor.ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2 + 1)
    bRefuseOk := bRefuseOk and (eAbove == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and bRampEquals(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)
    motor.getError()                                        ' drain the refusals' recorded code
    debug("T0-5,refuse,below,", sdec_(eBelow), ",negative,", sdec_(eNegative), ",above,", sdec_(eAbove), ",unchanged,", zstr_(bRefuseOk ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

    eAnchor := motor.setAcceleration(ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2)
    stepAnchor, bAnchorOk := constRampStep(@"anchor", ACCEL_ANCHOR_MM_S2, eAnchor, decrDef)
    bAnchorOk := bAnchorOk and (abs(stepAnchor - minDef) <= minDef / ACCEL_ANCHOR_TOL_DIV)
    eTop := motor.setAcceleration(motor.ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2)
    stepTop, bTopOk := constRampStep(@"top", motor.ACCEL_MAX_MM_S2, eTop, decrDef)
    bTopOk := bTopOk and (stepTop > stepAnchor)

    eRestore := motor.setRampingValues(minDef, maxDef, incDef, decrDef)      ' later tests start this motor
    bPass := bRefuseOk and bAnchorOk and bTopOk and (eRestore == motor.NO_ERROR)
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-ACCEL", @sTaskPromises, @"NONE", @"MM_S2_CONST_RAMP", eAnchor <> motor.ERR_NO_WHEEL_DIA, bPass, ACCEL_CALLS_JUDGED)

PRI constRampStep(pLabel, rateMmS2, eAccel, decrWant) : rampStep, bConst
' Read back the ramp an accepted setAcceleration() left, judge that it is a constant ramp, and print it.
' One debug() record serves every rate T0-5 accepts.
'
' @param pLabel - pointer to the rate's name, printed as the line's tag ("anchor" or "top")
' @param rateMmS2 - the rate that was set, mm/s squared
' @param eAccel - setAcceleration()'s return for it
' @param decrWant - the ramp_down it must have left untouched
' @returns rampStep - the step it produced: ramp_min read back
' @returns bConst - TRUE when the call returned NO_ERROR and left ramp_min == ramp_max, ramp_inc 0, ramp_down untouched

    rampStep, _, _, _ := motor.getRampingValues()
    bConst := (eAccel == motor.NO_ERROR) and bRampEquals(rampStep, rampStep, 0, decrWant)
    debug("T0-5,", zstr_(pLabel), ",mm_s2,", sdec_(rateMmS2), ",status,", sdec_(eAccel), ",step,", sdec_(rampStep), ",constant,", zstr_(bConst ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))

PRI emitCellDecl(pCell, pTask)
' One SIGNOFF-DECL, from hub strings (see emitCellBool() for why).
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task number, as text

    debug("SIGNOFF-DECL,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask))

PRI emitCellBool(pCell, pTask, pMotor, pCrit, bMeasured, bPass, instCount)
' One BOOL SIGNOFF for a cell. The cell, motor and criterion names are hub strings rather than
' literals inside the debug() call, so every cell shares these two DEBUG records and their data -- this
' binary's DEBUG data is the budget PL-74's silent build ran close to (study F12), and each literal SIGNOFF
' line spends about 150 bytes of it.
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pTask - pointer to the owning todo-mcp task number, as text
' @param pMotor - pointer to the motor token (NONE, RIGHT, BOTH)
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the condition arose and bPass is a measurement
' @param bPass - the criterion held
' @param instCount - the claims the verdict covers, printed as n when measured

    if bMeasured
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask), ",motor,", zstr_(pMotor), ",crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,", udec_(instCount), ",verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,", zstr_(pTask), ",motor,", zstr_(pMotor), ",crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")

PRI bRampEquals(minWant, maxWant, incWant, decrWant) : bSame | minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp
' Report whether `motor`'s four ramping values read back exactly as given.
'
' @param minWant - expected ramp_min
' @param maxWant - expected ramp_max
' @param incWant - expected ramp_inc
' @param decrWant - expected ramp_down
' @returns bSame - TRUE when all four read back equal
'
' @local minRamp - ramp_min read back
' @local maxRamp - ramp_max read back
' @local incRamp - ramp_inc read back
' @local decrRamp - ramp_down read back

    minRamp, maxRamp, incRamp, decrRamp := motor.getRampingValues()
    bSame := (minRamp == minWant) and (maxRamp == maxWant) and (incRamp == incWant) and (decrRamp == decrWant)

PRI testT0_6() | resultKm, resultMi, rotResult, eRotCode, eStopDist, eStopCode
' I/T, K: getDistance(DDU_KM)/(DDU_MI) are valid units and return a value.
' getRotationCount(99) (99 is not a DRU_* unit) and stopAfterDistance(0,
' DDU_IN) (a zero distance) used to abort; under the error contract (task 3554)
' the getter returns its neutral 0 and records ERR_BAD_UNITS, and the command
' returns and records ERR_BAD_COUNT. The two codes feed R16-T0-NOABORT, judged
' in T0-7. UNFIXED: both calls aborted, which ended the run at main()'s trap
' and left the cell with no verdict.
'
' @local resultKm - getDistance(DDU_KM)'s return
' @local resultMi - getDistance(DDU_MI)'s return
' @local rotResult - getRotationCount(99)'s return (expected 0)
' @local eRotCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BAD_UNITS)
' @local eStopDist - stopAfterDistance(0, DDU_IN)'s return (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eStopCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)

    motor.getError()                                        ' start from a clear slot
    resultKm := motor.getDistance(motor.DDU_KM)
    debug("T0-6,call,getDistance_KM,result,", sdec_(resultKm))

    resultMi := motor.getDistance(motor.DDU_MI)
    debug("T0-6,call,getDistance_MI,result,", sdec_(resultMi))

    motor.getError()                                        ' the distance calls' own codes are not judged here
    rotResult := motor.getRotationCount(99)
    eRotCode := motor.getError()
    debug("T0-6,call,getRotationCount_99,result,", sdec_(rotResult), ",error,", sdec_(eRotCode))

    eStopDist := motor.stopAfterDistance(0, motor.DDU_IN)
    eStopCode := motor.getError()
    debug("T0-6,call,stopAfterDistance_0in,status,", sdec_(eStopDist), ",error,", sdec_(eStopCode))

    bUnitsCodesOk := (rotResult == 0) and (eRotCode == motor.ERR_BAD_UNITS) and (eStopDist == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and (eStopCode == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT)

PRI testT0_7() | eSetupA, eOverlap, eOverlapCode, eNonOverlap, bPass
' AE: two separate isp_bldc_motor instances, testSetup() on deliberately
' overlapping pin groups -- PINS_P0_P15 and PINS_P8_P23 overlap on P8-P15, the
' audit's own example. motorA claims P0-P15; motorB's overlapping testSetup()
' is refused: since the error contract (task 3554) it RETURNS
' ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE and records it, where it used to abort. No real board is
' wired to either base, so this only ever toggles unused pins briefly while
' probing for a board that is not there.
'
' AE's other half, the one that matters to shipped code: two motors on
' NON-overlapping ranges must still both initialise (motorB on P32_P47).
'
' R16-T0-NOABORT (task 3554): TRUE when T0-6's two codes were right AND
' motorA's claim returned NO_ERROR AND the overlap returned and recorded
' ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE AND the non-overlapping claim returned NO_ERROR. That this
' line prints at all is the "nothing aborted" half.
'
' T0-14a/T0-14b release motorA/motorB's claims made here (P0_P15, P32_P47)
' before they run, so this test's claims never leak into theirs.
'
' @local eSetupA - motorA.testSetup(P0_P15)'s status
' @local eOverlap - motorB.testSetup(P8_P23)'s status (expected ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE)
' @local eOverlapCode - motorB.getError() after it
' @local eNonOverlap - motorB.testSetup(P32_P47)'s status
' @local bPass - R16-T0-NOABORT's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-7,begin,left_base,P0_P15,right_base,P8_P23")
    motorA.getError()
    motorB.getError()
    eSetupA := motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    eOverlap := motorB.testSetup(motorB.PINS_P8_P23, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorB.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    eOverlapCode := motorB.getError()
    debug("T0-7,end,claim_status,", sdec_(eSetupA), ",overlap_status,", sdec_(eOverlap), ",overlap_error,", sdec_(eOverlapCode))

    debug("T0-7,nonoverlap,begin,held_base,P0_P15,new_base,P32_P47")
    eNonOverlap := motorB.testSetup(motorB.PINS_P32_P47, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorB.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    debug("T0-7,nonoverlap,end,status,", sdec_(eNonOverlap))
    motorA.getError()
    motorB.getError()

    bPass := bUnitsCodesOk and (eSetupA == motorA.NO_ERROR) and (eOverlap == motorB.ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE) and (eOverlapCode == motorB.ERR_PIN_GROUP_IN_USE) and (eNonOverlap == motorB.NO_ERROR)
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-NOABORT,task,3554,motor,NONE,crit,CODE_NOT_ABORT,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,4,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI spread5(pArr) : spreadVal | idx, mx, mn
' Helper for R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11): max - min of 5 LONGs at {pArr}.
'
' @param pArr - address of a 5-element LONG array
' @returns spreadVal - max(pArr[0..4]) - min(pArr[0..4])
' @local idx - loop index
' @local mx - running maximum
' @local mn - running minimum

    mx := LONG[pArr][0]
    mn := LONG[pArr][0]
    repeat idx from 1 to 4
        if LONG[pArr][idx] > mx
            mx := LONG[pArr][idx]
        if LONG[pArr][idx] < mn
            mn := LONG[pArr][idx]
    spreadVal := mx - mn

PRI emitZxsSignoff(pCritStr, measuredSpread, validCount)
' Helper for R8-T0-ZXS (T0-11): emit one channel's SIGNOFF record. NOMEAS with n = validCount
' when fewer than 5 valid lifetimes were captured (design SS A.5-e); the 5-of-5 path prints
' measuredSpread against SF_ZXS_LO..SF_ZXS_HI. A genuine abort during T0-11 is caught by main()'s
' single top-level trap (task 3539), which ends the whole run before this is even reached.
'
' Worst-case bytes for this line ("R8-T0-ZXS"/"ZXS_I".."ZXS_W", motor RIGHT,
' measured up to -2_147_483_648, n 5, verdict FAIL): counted by hand at 130
' bytes, well under the 255-byte per-debug() limit (test_bench_detect.spin2
' header) and under design SS B.2's general 193-byte bound.
'
' @param pCritStr - pointer to "ZXS_I"/"ZXS_U"/"ZXS_V"/"ZXS_W"
' @param measuredSpread - spread5()'s result for this channel (ignored, NA, when validCount < 5)
' @param validCount - number of valid lifetimes captured (0..5)

    if validCount == 5
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCritStr), ",measured,", sdec_(measuredSpread), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_HI), ",units,MV_X10,n,5,verdict,", zstr_(((measuredSpread >= SF_ZXS_LO) and (measuredSpread <= SF_ZXS_HI)) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R8-T0-ZXS,task,3529,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCritStr), ",measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_ZXS_HI), ",units,MV_X10,n,", udec_(validCount), ",verdict,NOMEAS")

PRI testT0_11() | cycleIdx, validCount, startResult, rawMotorCog, readyMs, sampleIdx, sumI, sumU, sumV, sumW, meanI[5], meanU[5], meanV[5], meanW[5], nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, nSenseU, nSenseV, nSenseW, eDrvrState, bDidFault, bValid, spreadI, spreadU, spreadV, spreadW
' R8-T0-ZXS (task 3529), design SS H.1: 5 cycles of start() -> wait ready
' (<= 2000 ms, T0 has no watchdog) -> 200 samples x 5 ms of testGetTelemetry()
' i/u/v/w at zero command (start() leaves the command at zero, drive floated)
' -> stop() -> 500 ms rest. Per channel: max - min of the 5 lifetime means
' (in mV x10) is the measured value; fewer than 5 valid lifetimes is NOMEAS.
'
' PL-21: telemetry is read only while `motor`'s own driver cog is actually
' running (start() succeeded AND isReady() went TRUE within the 2000 ms
' budget) -- otherwise this cycle contributes no lifetime at all, exactly
' the frozen-telemetry hazard PL-21 documents.
'
' Accumulator bound: sense_*_mV is a millivolt reading against the driver's
' 3300 mV ADC scale (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2617, numerator = 3300 mV << 11),
' so |sense_x_mV| <= 5000 with generous margin. Over 200 samples,
' |sumX| <= 200 * 5000 = 1_000_000, and |sumX * 10| <= 10_000_000 -- both
' comfortably inside the 32-bit signed range (+-2_147_483_647).
'
' start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): it returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 on
' failure, neither of which is an abort. POSITIVE CONTROL (P4): bValid also requires
' testGetMotorCog() to independently read back startResult + 1 -- the same cross-check T0-15a
' uses -- so a stuck value cannot satisfy this cell by accident; a real abort is caught by
' main()'s single top-level trap instead.
'
' @local cycleIdx - 0..4, which of the 5 start()/stop() cycles
' @local validCount - number of cycles that produced a valid lifetime (0..5)
' @local startResult - start()'s return for this cycle
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot right after start(), the positive control
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms
' @local sampleIdx - 0..199, which telemetry sample within a lifetime
' @local sumI - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_i_mV samples (see bound above)
' @local sumU - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_u_mV samples
' @local sumV - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_v_mV samples
' @local sumW - per-lifetime accumulator of sense_w_mV samples
' @local meanI - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_i_mV, in mV x10
' @local meanU - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_u_mV, in mV x10
' @local meanV - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_v_mV, in mV x10
' @local meanW - the up-to-5 lifetime means of sense_w_mV, in mV x10
' @local nDuty - testGetTelemetry()'s duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - testGetTelemetry()'s error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_i_mV sample
' @local nSenseU - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_u_mV sample
' @local nSenseV - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_v_mV sample
' @local nSenseW - testGetTelemetry()'s sense_w_mV sample
' @local eDrvrState - testGetTelemetry()'s DCS_* sample (unused here)
' @local bDidFault - testGetTelemetry()'s fault sample (unused here)
' @local bValid - TRUE when this cycle's start() succeeded, went ready in time, and cross-checked
' @local spreadI - spread5()'s result for the I channel (NA when validCount < 5)
' @local spreadU - spread5()'s result for the U channel (NA when validCount < 5)
' @local spreadV - spread5()'s result for the V channel (NA when validCount < 5)
' @local spreadW - spread5()'s result for the W channel (NA when validCount < 5)

    debug("T0-11,begin")
    validCount := 0
    repeat cycleIdx from 0 to 4
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        bValid := (startResult >= 0) and motor.isReady() and (rawMotorCog == startResult + 1)
        if bValid
            sumI := 0
            sumU := 0
            sumV := 0
            sumW := 0
            repeat sampleIdx from 0 to 199
                nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, nSenseU, nSenseV, nSenseW, eDrvrState, bDidFault := motor.testGetTelemetry()
                sumI += nSenseI
                sumU += nSenseU
                sumV += nSenseV
                sumW += nSenseW
                waitms(5)
            meanI[validCount] := (sumI * 10) / 200
            meanU[validCount] := (sumU * 10) / 200
            meanV[validCount] := (sumV * 10) / 200
            meanW[validCount] := (sumW * 10) / 200
            debug("T0-11,lifetime,", udec_(validCount), ",mean_i_x10,", sdec_(meanI[validCount]), ",mean_u_x10,", sdec_(meanU[validCount]), ",mean_v_x10,", sdec_(meanV[validCount]), ",mean_w_x10,", sdec_(meanW[validCount]))
            validCount += 1
        else
            debug("T0-11,cycle,", udec_(cycleIdx), ",skipped,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog))
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()
        waitms(500)

    if validCount == 5
        spreadI := spread5(@meanI)
        spreadU := spread5(@meanU)
        spreadV := spread5(@meanV)
        spreadW := spread5(@meanW)
    debug("T0-11,end,valid_lifetimes,", udec_(validCount))
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_I", spreadI, validCount)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_U", spreadU, validCount)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_V", spreadV, validCount)
    emitZxsSignoff(@"ZXS_W", spreadW, validCount)

PRI testT0_13() | startResult, rawMotorCog, readyMs, missedCount, illegalCount, sumCounts, bReady, bPass
' R3-T0-STOPPED (task 3501), design SS H.1: start at zero command, wait ready
' (<= 2000 ms), hold 1000 ms, read both hall integrity counts. measured =
' missed + illegal; a stationary motor's hall code never transitions, so the
' criterion is exactly 0.
' start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): it returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 on
' failure, neither of which is an abort; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
' top-level trap. POSITIVE CONTROL (P4): the ready branch also requires testGetMotorCog() to
' independently read back startResult + 1, so a stuck value cannot satisfy this cell.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot right after start(), the positive control
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms
' @local missedCount - getHallIntegrityCounts()'s nMissedTransitions
' @local illegalCount - getHallIntegrityCounts()'s nIllegalCodes
' @local sumCounts - missedCount + illegalCount, this cell's measured value
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reached ready within budget
' @local bPass - this cell's verdict

    debug("T0-13,begin")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    readyMs := 0
    repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
        waitms(10)
        readyMs += 10
    bReady := motor.isReady()
    if (startResult >= 0) and bReady and (rawMotorCog == startResult + 1)
        waitms(1000)
        missedCount, illegalCount := motor.getHallIntegrityCounts()
        sumCounts := missedCount + illegalCount
        bPass := (sumCounts == SF_STOP_LO)
        debug("T0-13,end,missed,", udec_(missedCount), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount))
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501,motor,NONE,crit,STOPPED_COUNTS,measured,", sdec_(sumCounts), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_STOP_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_STOP_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("T0-13,end,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog))
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R3-T0-STOPPED,task,3501,motor,NONE,crit,STOPPED_COUNTS,measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_STOP_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_STOP_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14a() | baseIdx, pinBase, iter, eBoardRev, notRevBCount, pMotorTok
' R2-T0-REPEAT (task 3500): 32 x testSetup() + getBoardType() on each
' populated base, P16 and P32. motorA/motorB are stopped first so T0-7's pin
' claims are released before this test claims the same bases. testSetup() is
' called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
' top-level trap.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 (T0_MOTOR_BASE) or 1 (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test this iteration
' @local iter - 0..31, which of the 32 reads
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return for this read
' @local notRevBCount - this base's measured value: reads that were not REV_B
' @local pMotorTok - "RIGHT" for P16, "LEFT" for P32 (the bench boards), the record's motor field

    debug("T0-14,begin,repeat")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"
        notRevBCount := 0
        repeat iter from 0 to 31
            motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
            eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
            if eBoardRev <> motor.REV_B
                notRevBCount += 1
        debug("T0-14a,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",not_revb_count,", udec_(notRevBCount))
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-REPEAT,task,3500,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,READS_NOT_REVB,measured,", sdec_(notRevBCount), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_REPEAT_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_REPEAT_HI), ",units,COUNT,n,32,verdict,", zstr_((notRevBCount == 0) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14b() | baseIdx, pinBase, otherBase, deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt, pinAdcX, eBoardRev, startResult, readyMs, bDirtyIsRevB, pMotorTok
' R2-T0-DIRTY (task 3500), design SS H.1: on each populated base, an
' initialised but NOT running group. The harness itself drives base+4 into
' the driver's own steady-state ADC sampling mode -- adc_modes+2 =
' p_adc_1x | p_count_highs, WRPIN'd onto adc_pins at isp_bldc_motor.spin2:2913
' (mode constants at :2633..2635); the matching count period is adc_fram,
' WXPIN'd at :2909, and this test reads adc_fram back through the existing
' testGetDriveConstants() getter rather than recomputing it -- then leaves
' the pin with DIR low (pinfloat(), which per spin2-authoring-guide.md:1270
' clears DIR only and leaves the WRPIN mode set), exactly the state an idle
' driver cog would
' leave it in without the "defensive clear" getBoardType() performs (its own
' pinclear() at :900 when motorCog == 0). measured TRUE when the read that
' follows is REV_B; this is the cell that FAILs if that defensive clear ever
' regresses.
'
' Also: start() -> ready -> stop() on the same group, then start the OTHER
' group on motorA in between (to confirm it stays clean of this group's
' state), then testSetup()+getBoardType() again on the original group.
' Printed as T0-14b CSV lines; not a separate sign-off instance (design
' SS H.1 states one SIGNOFF per base for this cell).
'
' testSetup() and start() below are all called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught
' by main()'s single top-level trap instead.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 (T0_MOTOR_BASE) or 1 (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test this iteration
' @local otherBase - the other populated base, started on motorA in between
' @local deadGap - dead_gap, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local pwmLimit - pwm_limit, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local dutyMin - duty_min, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local dutyMax - duty_max, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local adcFrame - adc_fram, the ADC sample period matching the PWM frame width (programmed into the ADC pin)
' @local frameCnt - frame_cnt, from testGetDriveConstants() (unused here)
' @local pinAdcX - pinBase + 4, the detection/ADC-common pin
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return, read twice per base
' @local startResult - start()'s return for the confirm cycle
' @local readyMs - ready-wait accumulator, bounded at 2000 ms, reused for both confirm starts
' @local bDirtyIsRevB - this base's measured value: the dirty-pin read was REV_B
' @local pMotorTok - "RIGHT" for P16, "LEFT" for P32 (the bench boards), the record's motor field

    debug("T0-14,begin,dirty")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            otherBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            otherBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"

        motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := motor.testGetDriveConstants()
        pinAdcX := pinBase + 4

        wrpin(pinAdcX, P_ADC_1X | P_COUNT_HIGHS)
        wxpin(pinAdcX, adcFrame)
        pinfloat(pinAdcX)                              ' DIR low; PINFLOAT() clears DIR only, the WRPIN mode survives (spin2-authoring-guide.md:1270)

        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        bDirtyIsRevB := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_B)
        debug("T0-14b,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",dirty_read,", udec_(eBoardRev))

        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startResult := motor.start(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motor.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()

        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motorA.start(otherBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        readyMs := 0
        repeat while (motorA.isReady() == FALSE) and (readyMs < 2000)
            waitms(10)
            readyMs += 10
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motorA.stop()

        motor.testSetup(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
        debug("T0-14b,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",poststart_read,", udec_(eBoardRev))

        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-DIRTY,task,3500,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,POSTSTOP_REVB,measured,", zstr_(bDirtyIsRevB ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bDirtyIsRevB ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_14c() | eBoardRev, bEmpty
' R2-T0-EMPTY (task 3500): testSetup(PINS_P0_P15) + getBoardType(). measured
' TRUE when it reads REV_Unknown. NEVER probe PINS_P40_P55: its sense pin P44
' is the LEFT board's pin_pwm_w_l (32 + 12), and T0 runs with the rail on --
' getBoardType() drives it high for 1 ms (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:889-890,
' hazard also recorded at test_bench_detect.spin2:161-165). testSetup() is
' called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
' top-level trap.
'
' @local eBoardRev - getBoardType()'s return
' @local bEmpty - this cell's measured value: the read was REV_Unknown

    debug("T0-14,begin,empty")
    motor.testSetup(motor.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    eBoardRev := motor.getBoardType()
    bEmpty := (eBoardRev == motor.REV_Unknown)
    debug("T0-14c,base,P0_P15,read,", udec_(eBoardRev))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R2-T0-EMPTY,task,3500,motor,NONE,crit,EMPTY_NODET,measured,", zstr_(bEmpty ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bEmpty ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15a() | startResult, rawMotorCog, bPass
' R1-T0-START (task 3499): start() on P16, called UNTRAPPED (task 3539) --
' it returns a cog id 0..7 on success or -1 on failure, neither of which is
' an abort; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single top-level trap. The
' return must be in 0..7 and equal testGetMotorCog() - 1. A BOOL cell (task
' 3537): measured is TRUE only when both hold; the two raw numbers are on the
' T0-15a line. testGetMotorCog() is ALSO this cell's positive control (P4):
' it is read independently of start()'s own return, so a stuck value cannot
' satisfy the cell by accident.
'
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot, taken right after start()
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,start")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    bPass := (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI) and (startResult == rawMotorCog - 1)
    debug("T0-15a,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-START,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,RET_EQ_COG_M1,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15c() | baseline, startResult1, free1, startResult2, rawMotorCog2, free2, free3, diffFree, bPass
' R1-T0-RESTART (task 3499): count free cogs (baseline) -> start() -> free1 ->
' start() again with NO stop() -> free2 -> stop() -> free3. A BOOL cell (task
' 3537): measured is TRUE only when |free2 - free1| + |free3 - baseline| == 0
' AND free1 == baseline - SF_START_COGS (PL-24: a second start() must not orphan
' the first start's cogs; task 3513: a start() is the driver plus its front cog,
' so this is also the single-motor fixed-cog-count cell -- UNFIXED, start()
' alone took 1 cog and this term FAILs); the four free-cog counts are on the
' T0-15c line. T0-15d reads
' state immediately after this test's own stop(), so it must be called right
' after this one from runTier0Tests().
' Both start()s are called UNTRAPPED (task 3539); a genuine abort is caught
' by main()'s single top-level trap. POSITIVE CONTROL (P4): the second
' start()'s testGetMotorCog() readback must independently agree with its own
' return, so a stuck value on either start() cannot satisfy this cell.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before either start()
' @local startResult1 - first start()'s return
' @local free1 - free cogs after the first start()
' @local startResult2 - second start()'s return, no intervening stop()
' @local rawMotorCog2 - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the second start(), the positive control
' @local free2 - free cogs after the second start()
' @local free3 - free cogs after this test's stop()
' @local diffFree - abs(free2-free1) + abs(free3-baseline), one of this cell's two conditions
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-15,begin,restart")
    bRestartStopValid := FALSE
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult1 := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    free1 := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult2 := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog2 := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    free2 := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    bRestartStopValid := (startResult1 >= 0) and (startResult2 >= 0) and (rawMotorCog2 == startResult2 + 1)
    free3 := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    diffFree := abs(free2 - free1) + abs(free3 - baseline)
    bPass := (diffFree == SF_RESTART_LO) and (free1 == baseline - SF_START_COGS)
    debug("T0-15c,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free1,", udec_(free1), ",start1,", sdec_(startResult1), ",free2,", udec_(free2), ",start2,", sdec_(startResult2), ",raw_motor_cog2,", sdec_(rawMotorCog2), ",free3,", udec_(free3))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-RESTART,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,NO_ORPHAN,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_15d() | bReady, bStopped, eState, bPass
' R10-T0-STOPREADY (task 3533): right after T0-15c's own stop() (this method
' must run immediately after testT0_15c() from runTier0Tests(), with no other
' call touching `motor` in between). measured TRUE when isReady() is FALSE
' AND isStopped() is FALSE (PL-28 item 2 / task 3533: stop() now leaves
' drv_state at DCS_Unknown, not stale). getDriverState() is logged beside the
' verdict; DCS_Unknown is expected.
' This cell judges the state T0-15c's own stop() left, so it is NOMEAS,n,0
' when either of T0-15c's start()s returned -1 or failed its positive
' control, or T0-15c never reached its stop() -- bRestartStopValid FALSE.
'
' @local bReady - motor.isReady()'s value right now
' @local bStopped - motor.isStopped()'s value right now
' @local eState - motor.getDriverState()'s value right now (expect DCS_Unknown)
' @local bPass - this cell's verdict

    bReady := motor.isReady()
    bStopped := motor.isStopped()
    eState := motor.getDriverState()
    bPass := (bReady == FALSE) and (bStopped == FALSE)
    debug("T0-15d,driver_state,", udec_(eState), ",ready,", zstr_(bReady ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",stopped,", zstr_(bStopped ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",t0_15c_valid,", zstr_(bRestartStopValid ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    if bRestartStopValid == FALSE
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R10-T0-STOPREADY,task,3533,motor,NONE,crit,STOP_NOT_READY,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R10-T0-STOPREADY,task,3533,motor,NONE,crit,STOP_NOT_READY,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI runExhaustionPhase() | baseline, cogsOccupied, heldCount, startT15, rawCogT15, startT22, codeT22, rawCogT22, freeAfter
' The three cog-exhaustion cells share ONE occupancy (PL-85: each used to start and stop seven spacers of
' its own, and every damaged record sat beside such a burst). One occupy burst, then T0-8 and T0-15b with
' every spare cog held; one spacer released so exactly one cog is free for T0-22's start; one release
' burst; then one free-cog count that both T0-15b and T0-22 judge (free_after == baseline, as before).
' Destructive: a start() that fails can leave the object half-initialised, so this runs last.

' Local Variables:
' @local baseline - free cogs before the occupancy
' @local cogsOccupied - spacers the occupancy started (every spare cog)
' @local heldCount - spacers held (every spare cog, then one fewer for T0-22)
' @local startT15 - T0-15b's start() return under total exhaustion
' @local rawCogT15 - testGetMotorCog() after T0-15b's start()
' @local startT22 - T0-22's start() return with one cog free
' @local codeT22 - getError() after T0-22's start()
' @local rawCogT22 - testGetMotorCog() after T0-22's start()
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after every spacer is released

    debug("T0-EXH,begin,one_occupancy,cells,T0-8,T0-15b,T0-22")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motorA.stop()
    motor.getError()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    cogsOccupied := occupySpacers(MAX_SPACER_COGS)
    heldCount := cogsOccupied

    testT0_8(heldCount)
    startT15, rawCogT15 := testT0_15bStart()

    heldCount := releaseOneSpacer(heldCount)
    startT22, codeT22, rawCogT22 := testT0_22Start()

    releaseSpacers(heldCount)
    freeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    debug("T0-EXH,end,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",held_for_t22,", udec_(heldCount), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter))

    testT0_15bJudge(cogsOccupied, baseline, startT15, rawCogT15, freeAfter)
    testT0_22Judge(baseline, heldCount, startT22, codeT22, rawCogT22, freeAfter)

PRI testT0_8(heldCount) | startResult
' C, AD: with every spare cog occupied (runExhaustionPhase()), call the real start() (not testSetup())
' and print its raw return. coginit() returns the documented $8000_xxxx form on failure, not a bare -1;
' start() itself returns -1 on failure specifically, which is what R1-T0-EXHAUST (T0-15b) checks. This
' test exists to print the raw value, not to judge it; R1-T0-EXHAUST is the harsher probe that also
' confirms no cog leaked.
'
' @param heldCount - spacers holding every spare cog

' Local Variables:
' @local startResult - start()'s raw return value under cog exhaustion, called UNTRAPPED
'                       (task 3539): cog exhaustion is a normal -1 return, not an abort, so
'                       nothing here needs a trap; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single
'                       top-level trap instead

    debug("T0-8,begin")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    debug("T0-8,end,cogs_occupied,", udec_(heldCount), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult))

    ' stop() unconditionally. A start() that returned -1 may STILL have gotten
    ' partway -- the 2026-09-10 run shows a driver cog reaching INIT on a call
    ' that reported failure -- so the object can be left half-initialised, and
    ' anything that starts it afterwards then fails too. Leave it clean.
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI spacerLoop()
' Idle forever -- exists only to occupy a cog so start() has none left (runExhaustionPhase()). It never
' prints and holds no lock, so it may be stopped at any moment.
'

    repeat
        waitms(1000)

PRI occupySpacers(maxCount) : heldCount | spareCogId
' Start up to maxCount spacer cogs and hold them in heldSpacerId[] until releaseSpacers(). The whole
' burst is one cog event: nothing prints until it ends.
'
' @param maxCount - the most spacers to start
' @returns heldCount - spacers now running

' Local Variables:
' @local spareCogId - cogspin()'s return for the current attempt

    heldCount := 0
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    repeat while heldCount < (maxCount <# MAX_SPACER_COGS)
        spareCogId := cogspin(NEWCOG, spacerLoop(), @spacerStacks[heldCount * SPACER_STACK_LONGS])
        if spareCogId < 0
            quit
        heldSpacerId[heldCount] := spareCogId
        heldCount += 1
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()

PRI releaseOneSpacer(heldCount) : stillHeld
' Stop the last spacer occupySpacers() started, freeing exactly one cog.
'
' @param heldCount - spacers held now
' @returns stillHeld - spacers held after this (heldCount - 1, or 0 when none was held)

    stillHeld := heldCount
    if stillHeld > 0
        stillHeld -= 1
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        cogstop(heldSpacerId[stillHeld])

PRI releaseSpacers(heldCount) | spacerIdx
' Stop the first heldCount spacers occupySpacers() started, as one cog event.
'
' @param heldCount - spacers to stop

' Local Variables:
' @local spacerIdx - index into heldSpacerId[]

    if heldCount > 0                                        ' repeat 0 to -1 would count down, not skip
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        repeat spacerIdx from 0 to heldCount - 1
            cogstop(heldSpacerId[spacerIdx])

PRI testT0_16() | baseline, startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog, freeAfter, bPass
' R16-T0-BADGROUP (task 3554, F-3): start() with a value that is not a PINS_* group. The error contract
' validates every argument before anything is acquired, so the call must return -1, record
' ERR_BAD_PIN_GROUP, launch no cog (testGetMotorCog() 0) and leave the free-cog count unchanged.
' UNFIXED: an illegal group launched a driver cog on pins derived from -1 (F-3).
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before the call
' @local startResult - start()'s return (expected -1)
' @local eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BAD_PIN_GROUP)
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after the call
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-16,begin,bad_group")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motorA.start(BAD_PIN_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    eCode := motorA.getError()
    rawMotorCog := motorA.testGetMotorCog()
    freeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    bPass := (startResult == -1) and (eCode == motorA.ERR_BAD_PIN_GROUP) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline)
    debug("T0-16,end,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",error,", sdec_(eCode), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-BADGROUP,task,3554,motor,NONE,crit,REJECT_NO_COG,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_17() | markPins, legalBase, dirBefore, startResult, dirAfter, bPass
' R16-T0-PINSKEEP (task 3554, PL-48): the release demo's order -- validBasePinForChoice() then start() on a
' fresh instance -- must not touch P8..P15, where demo_single_motor runs HDMI. The marker is this cog's own
' DIR bits for P8..P15, set through a 15 k pull-down (WRPIN P_LOW_15K, then PINLOW), so the marker drives
' nothing harder than a pull resistor. PINCLEAR clears DIR (p2kbSpin2Pinclear), and the unfixed chain ran
' pinclear(0 addpins 7) and pinclear(8 addpins 7) on THIS cog inside start()'s stop-first, so a cleared
' bit is the defect. motorP is an instance nothing else in this file has touched.
' UNFIXED: validBasePinForChoice() took the claim, start() then stop()ped first with pinbase still 0, and
' DIR bits 8..15 read 0 afterwards.
'
' @local markPins - the P8..P15 pin field
' @local legalBase - validBasePinForChoice()'s return
' @local dirBefore - DIR bits 8..15 after the marker is set (expected all set)
' @local startResult - motorP.start()'s return
' @local dirAfter - DIR bits 8..15 after start() and stop()
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-17,begin,pins_keep")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    markPins := PL48_MARK_BASE addpins PL48_MARK_SPAN
    wrpin(markPins, P_LOW_15K)
    pinlow(markPins)
    dirBefore := (DIRA >> PL48_MARK_SHIFT) & PL48_MARK_MASK
    legalBase := motorP.validBasePinForChoice(T0_MOTOR_BASE)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motorP.start(legalBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorP.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    motorP.stop()
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    dirAfter := (DIRA >> PL48_MARK_SHIFT) & PL48_MARK_MASK
    pinclear(markPins)
    bPass := (dirBefore == PL48_MARK_MASK) and (dirAfter == PL48_MARK_MASK) and (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI)
    debug("T0-17,end,legal_base,", sdec_(legalBase), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",dir_before,", uhex_(dirBefore), ",dir_after,", uhex_(dirAfter))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-PINSKEEP,task,3554,motor,RIGHT,crit,P8_P15_UNTOUCHED,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_18() | eDist, eTime, eOwn, eLeft, eRight, bPass
' R16-T0-STRNOTSTART (task 3555, F-5c): stop limits on a steering object that was never started. start()
' would erase them, so each is refused: stopAfterDistance() and stopAfterTime() must return
' ERR_NOT_STARTED, and getError()'s first (steering) result must name it. Nothing moves: no cog exists.
' UNFIXED: both calls returned nothing and silently armed a limit start() then erased (F-5c).
'
' @local eDist - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_M)'s return
' @local eTime - stopAfterTime(1, DTU_SEC)'s return
' @local eOwn - getError()'s steering result
' @local eLeft - getError()'s left-wheel result (not judged; printed)
' @local eRight - getError()'s right-wheel result (not judged; printed)
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-18,begin,steer_not_started")
    steer.getError()
    eDist := steer.stopAfterDistance(1, steer.DDU_M)
    eTime := steer.stopAfterTime(1, steer.DTU_SEC)
    eOwn, eLeft, eRight := steer.getError()
    bPass := (eDist == motor.ERR_NOT_STARTED) and (eTime == motor.ERR_NOT_STARTED) and (eOwn == motor.ERR_NOT_STARTED)
    debug("T0-18,end,dist_status,", sdec_(eDist), ",time_status,", sdec_(eTime), ",error,", sdec_(eOwn), ",left_error,", sdec_(eLeft), ",right_error,", sdec_(eRight))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-STRNOTSTART,task,3555,motor,BOTH,crit,LIMIT_REFUSED,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,2,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_19() | baseline, startResult, freeRunning, freeStopped, bPass, voltBefore, milliVoltsBefore, voltRunning, milliVoltsRunning, bVoltOk
' R16-T0-STEERCOGS (task 3513): the two-wheel form costs 3 cogs -- two owned drivers and one steering front
' cog -- and stop() returns all of them. The start commands zero speed on both wheels, so nothing turns.
' NOT A DISCRIMINATOR, and stated as such: the unfixed two-wheel shape was also 3 cogs (two drivers plus
' the sense task). The single-motor form, which did change (1 -> 2), is judged by R1-T0-RESTART.
'
' AK / R17-T0-VOLTGET (task 3577): getDriveVoltage() returns the PWR_* value start() was given
' (user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE) and its nominal mV (SF_PACK_MV). The motor object's answer is T0-3's read of its running
' motor; the steering object's must agree while running, and be PWR_Unknown and 0 before its first start().
' Those reads start and stop nothing, and the final getError() drains the not-started code the first records.
' The unfixed library had no such getter, so this cell is COVERAGE of a new member rather than a before/after
' discriminator: it FAILs on a wrong mapping, on a steering forward that disagrees with the wheel, or on a
' not-started answer that claims a voltage. NOMEAS when T0-3's motor never reached ready.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before start()
' @local startResult - steer.start()'s return (the front cog id, 0..7)
' @local freeRunning - free cogs while started
' @local freeStopped - free cogs after stop()
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict
' @local voltBefore - steer.getDriveVoltage() before start(): the PWR_* value (expected PWR_Unknown)
' @local milliVoltsBefore - its mV (expected 0)
' @local voltRunning - steer.getDriveVoltage() while running: the PWR_* value
' @local milliVoltsRunning - its mV
' @local bVoltOk - R17-T0-VOLTGET's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-19,begin,steer_cogs")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    motorA.stop()
    motorB.stop()
    motorP.stop()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    voltBefore, milliVoltsBefore := steer.getDriveVoltage()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := steer.start(T0_SECOND_BASE, T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    freeRunning := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    voltRunning, milliVoltsRunning := steer.getDriveVoltage()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    steer.stop()
    freeStopped := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    steer.getError()
    bPass := (startResult >= SF_COG_LO) and (startResult <= SF_COG_HI) and (freeRunning == baseline - SF_STEER_COGS) and (freeStopped == baseline)
    debug("T0-19,end,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_running,", udec_(freeRunning), ",free_stopped,", udec_(freeStopped))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-STEERCOGS,task,3513,motor,BOTH,crit,THREE_COGS_RETURNED,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

    bVoltOk := (motorVolt == user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE) and (motorMilliVolts == SF_PACK_MV) and (startResult >= SF_COG_LO)
    bVoltOk := bVoltOk and (voltBefore == motor.PWR_Unknown) and (milliVoltsBefore == 0)
    bVoltOk := bVoltOk and (voltRunning == motorVolt) and (milliVoltsRunning == motorMilliVolts)
    debug("T0-19,volt,motor,", sdec_(motorVolt), ",mv,", sdec_(motorMilliVolts), ",steer_before,", sdec_(voltBefore), ",mv,", sdec_(milliVoltsBefore), ",steer_running,", sdec_(voltRunning), ",mv,", sdec_(milliVoltsRunning))
    emitCellBool(@"R17-T0-VOLTGET", @sTaskPromises, @"BOTH", @"CONFIGURED_VOLTAGE", bMotorVoltRead, bVoltOk, VOLT_READS_JUDGED)

PRI testT0_20() | baseIdx, pinBase, pMotorTok, startResult, sampleIdx, ampsSum, amps, meanAmps, pVerdict
' R16-T0-RESTZERO (task 3556, PL-45): getCurrent() at rest reads near 0 on each board. start() samples the
' floated rest zero (~1 s) and getCurrent() nets it out; this averages REST_SAMPLES readings at zero command
' and judges the mean against SF_REST_LO..SF_REST_HI (0.1 mA units). UNFIXED: the LEFT board read about 535
' (0.05 A, Visit 1). The RIGHT board's unfixed offset (~27) already sits inside the band, so only the LEFT
' instance discriminates; that is stated here and in the run sheet.
'
' @local baseIdx - 0 RIGHT (T0_MOTOR_BASE), 1 LEFT (T0_SECOND_BASE)
' @local pinBase - the base under test
' @local pMotorTok - the record's motor field
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local sampleIdx - sample loop counter
' @local ampsSum - sum of the readings
' @local amps - one getCurrent() reading, 0.1 mA units
' @local meanAmps - the instance's measured value
' @local pVerdict - PASS, FAIL or NOMEAS

    repeat baseIdx from 0 to 1
        if baseIdx == 0
            pinBase := T0_MOTOR_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"RIGHT"
        else
            pinBase := T0_SECOND_BASE
            pMotorTok := @"LEFT"
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        startResult := motor.start(pinBase, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
        benchLog.cogEventEnd()
        if bWaitReady(startResult)
            ampsSum := 0
            repeat sampleIdx from 1 to REST_SAMPLES
                waitms(REST_SAMPLE_MS)
                amps, _ := motor.getCurrent()
                ampsSum += amps
            meanAmps := ampsSum / REST_SAMPLES
            pVerdict := ((meanAmps >= SF_REST_LO) and (meanAmps <= SF_REST_HI)) ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"
            debug("T0-20,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",mean_amps_x10k,", sdec_(meanAmps))
            debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-RESTZERO,task,3556,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,REST_AMPS_X10K,measured,", sdec_(meanAmps), ",lo,", sdec_(SF_REST_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_REST_HI), ",units,AMPS_X10K,n,", udec_(REST_SAMPLES), ",verdict,", zstr_(pVerdict))
        else
            debug("T0-20,base,", udec_(pinBase), ",not_ready,start_return,", sdec_(startResult))
            debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-RESTZERO,task,3556,motor,", zstr_(pMotorTok), ",crit,REST_AMPS_X10K,measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(SF_REST_LO), ",hi,", sdec_(SF_REST_HI), ",units,AMPS_X10K,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")
        benchLog.cogEventBegin()
        motor.stop()
    motor.getError()

PRI testT0_21() | eSetup, amps, watts, eCode, bPass
' R16-T0-NOBOARD (task 3556, PL-25): getCurrent() on a group with no board (P0_P15, the empty group R2-T0-EMPTY
' already probes) returns its documented neutral 0 A / 0 mW and records ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED.
' UNFIXED: nothing was recorded, and a nonzero sense reading divided by -1 read negative. The recorded code
' is the discriminating half: with no driver running the hub sense long is 0 either way.
'
' @local eSetup - motorA.testSetup(P0_P15)'s status
' @local amps - getCurrent()'s current
' @local watts - getCurrent()'s power
' @local eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED)
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-21,begin,no_board")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    eSetup := motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    motorA.getError()
    amps, watts := motorA.getCurrent()
    eCode := motorA.getError()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    bPass := (eSetup == motorA.NO_ERROR) and (amps == 0) and (watts == 0) and (eCode == motorA.ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED)
    debug("T0-21,end,setup_status,", sdec_(eSetup), ",amps,", sdec_(amps), ",watts,", sdec_(watts), ",error,", sdec_(eCode))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-NOBOARD,task,3556,motor,NONE,crit,ZERO_AND_CODE,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI testT0_22Start() : startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog
' R16-T0-FRONTFAIL (task 3513), the start: runExhaustionPhase() holds all but one cog, so the driver takes
' the last one and the front cog cannot launch. testT0_22Judge() judges it once the spacers are released.
'
' @returns startResult - start()'s return (expected -1)
' @returns eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_NO_FREE_COG)
' @returns rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)

    debug("T0-22,begin,front_fail")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    eCode := motor.getError()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()

PRI testT0_22Judge(baseline, heldCount, startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog, freeAfter) | eClaim, bMeasured, bPass
' R16-T0-FRONTFAIL (task 3513): a start() with exactly one free cog. The driver takes it, the front cog
' cannot launch, and the start must undo itself: return -1, record ERR_NO_FREE_COG, leave no driver
' (testGetMotorCog() 0), give every cog back, and release the pin claim so another instance can take the
' group (motorA.testSetup() on the same group returns NO_ERROR -- PL-36's release, on the new failure
' path). NOMEAS when the spacers could not leave exactly one cog free. Nothing turns: the driver that
' briefly runs commands zero.
' UNFIXED: one cog was enough for start(), which returned a cog id, so the cell FAILs on the return.
'
' @param baseline - free cogs before the spacers
' @param heldCount - spacers held across the start
' @param startResult - start()'s return (expected -1)
' @param eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_NO_FREE_COG)
' @param rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)
' @param freeAfter - free cogs after the spacers are released

' Local Variables:
' @local eClaim - motorA.testSetup() on the same group (expected NO_ERROR)
' @local bMeasured - the spacers left exactly one cog free
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    eClaim := motorA.testSetup(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()
    bMeasured := (heldCount == baseline - 1)
    bPass := (startResult == -1) and (eCode == motor.ERR_NO_FREE_COG) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline) and (eClaim == motorA.NO_ERROR)
    debug("T0-22,end,baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",held,", udec_(heldCount), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",error,", sdec_(eCode), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter), ",claim_status,", sdec_(eClaim))
    if bMeasured
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-FRONTFAIL,task,3513,motor,RIGHT,crit,UNDO_NO_LEAK,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R16-T0-FRONTFAIL,task,3513,motor,RIGHT,crit,UNDO_NO_LEAK,measured,NA,lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")

PRI testT0_23() | baseline, startResult, eCode, rawMotorCog, freeAfter, eClaim, bPass
' R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART (task 3570, PL-73): start() on a group with no board (P0_P15, the empty group R2-T0-EMPTY
' already probes), auto-detecting, must be refused: return -1, record ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED, leave no driver
' (testGetMotorCog() 0), take no cog, and release the pin claim (motorA.testSetup() on the same group returns
' NO_ERROR). A board is driven only when detected or forced, because without its revision there is no current
' limit. Nothing is ever driven: the refusal comes before any cog is launched.
' UNFIXED: the start succeeded -- a driver ran on the empty group with no current limit -- so the cell FAILs on
' the return, the recorded code and the cog count.
'
' @local baseline - free cogs before the start
' @local startResult - motorA.start()'s return (expected -1)
' @local eCode - getError() after it (expected ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED)
' @local rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog() after it (expected 0)
' @local freeAfter - free cogs after it (expected baseline)
' @local eClaim - motorA.testSetup() on the same group afterwards (expected NO_ERROR: the claim was released)
' @local bPass - the cell's measured value and verdict

    debug("T0-23,begin,no_board_start")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    baseline := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motorA.start(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    eCode := motorA.getError()
    rawMotorCog := motorA.testGetMotorCog()
    freeAfter := benchLog.countFreeCogs()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    eClaim := motorA.testSetup(motorA.PINS_P0_P15, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motorA.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motorA.stop()
    motorA.getError()
    bPass := (startResult == -1) and (eCode == motorA.ERR_BOARD_NOT_DETECTED) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline) and (eClaim == motorA.NO_ERROR)
    debug("T0-23,end,start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",error,", sdec_(eCode), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter), ",claim_status,", sdec_(eClaim))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R17-T0-NOBOARDSTART,task,3570,motor,NONE,crit,REFUSED_NO_LEAK,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

PRI bUnitsKmMiOk() : bKmMiOk | eKm, ticksKm, eM, ticksM, eMi, ticksMi, eFt, ticksFt, eCmdKm, armedKm, eCmdMi, armedMi, eHuge, eCmdHuge, keptHuge
' K / R17-T0-KMMI (task 3577), on T0-3's running motor at zero command: kilometres and miles are distance units a
' caller can COMMAND. ticksForDistance() gives 1 km exactly the ticks of M_PER_KM metres and 1 mi exactly those of
' FT_PER_MI feet; stopAfterDistance() accepts both units and arms exactly those ticks; and a distance too large for
' a long is refused with ERR_BAD_COUNT, leaving the armed limit in place. Nothing turns: the limit is armed at rest.
' UNFIXED: the conversion had no KM or MI, so every such call returned ERR_BAD_UNITS and this FAILs at once.
'
' @returns bKmMiOk - TRUE when every conversion, command and refusal held
'
' @local eKm - ticksForDistance(1, DDU_KM)'s status
' @local ticksKm - its ticks
' @local eM - ticksForDistance(M_PER_KM, DDU_M)'s status
' @local ticksM - its ticks
' @local eMi - ticksForDistance(1, DDU_MI)'s status
' @local ticksMi - its ticks
' @local eFt - ticksForDistance(FT_PER_MI, DDU_FT)'s status
' @local ticksFt - its ticks
' @local eCmdKm - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_KM)'s status
' @local armedKm - the armed limit after it
' @local eCmdMi - stopAfterDistance(1, DDU_MI)'s status
' @local armedMi - the armed limit after it
' @local eHuge - ticksForDistance(POSX, DDU_KM)'s status (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local eCmdHuge - stopAfterDistance(POSX, DDU_MI)'s status (expected ERR_BAD_COUNT)
' @local keptHuge - the armed limit after it (expected armedMi)

    eKm, ticksKm := motor.ticksForDistance(1, motor.DDU_KM)
    eM, ticksM := motor.ticksForDistance(M_PER_KM, motor.DDU_M)
    eCmdKm := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, motor.DDU_KM)
    armedKm := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    eMi, ticksMi := motor.ticksForDistance(1, motor.DDU_MI)
    eFt, ticksFt := motor.ticksForDistance(FT_PER_MI, motor.DDU_FT)
    eCmdMi := motor.stopAfterDistance(1, motor.DDU_MI)
    armedMi := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    eHuge, _ := motor.ticksForDistance(POSX, motor.DDU_KM)
    eCmdHuge := motor.stopAfterDistance(POSX, motor.DDU_MI)
    keptHuge := motor.testGetStopHallTicks()
    motor.getError()                                        ' drain the refusal's recorded code
    bKmMiOk := bUnitOk(@"km", eKm, ticksKm, eM, ticksM, eCmdKm, armedKm)
    bKmMiOk := bUnitOk(@"mi", eMi, ticksMi, eFt, ticksFt, eCmdMi, armedMi) and bKmMiOk
    bKmMiOk := bKmMiOk and (eHuge == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and (eCmdHuge == motor.ERR_BAD_COUNT) and (keptHuge == armedMi)
    debug("T0-3,huge,status,", sdec_(eHuge), ",cmd_status,", sdec_(eCmdHuge), ",kept,", sdec_(keptHuge))

PRI bUnitOk(pUnit, eUnit, ticksUnit, eRef, ticksRef, eCmd, armedTicks) : bOk
' Judge and print one large unit: its conversion equals its exact equivalent in a smaller unit, and commanding it
' arms exactly those ticks. One debug() record serves both units.
'
' @param pUnit - pointer to the unit's name, printed as the line's tag ("km" or "mi")
' @param eUnit - ticksForDistance(1, unit)'s status
' @param ticksUnit - its ticks
' @param eRef - ticksForDistance() of the same distance in the smaller unit: its status
' @param ticksRef - its ticks
' @param eCmd - stopAfterDistance(1, unit)'s status
' @param armedTicks - the armed limit after it
' @returns bOk - TRUE when every call returned NO_ERROR and all three tick counts agree

    bOk := (eUnit == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eRef == motor.NO_ERROR) and (eCmd == motor.NO_ERROR)
    bOk := bOk and (ticksUnit == ticksRef) and (armedTicks == ticksUnit)
    debug("T0-3,", zstr_(pUnit), ",status,", sdec_(eUnit), ",ticks,", sdec_(ticksUnit), ",ref_status,", sdec_(eRef), ",ref_ticks,", sdec_(ticksRef), ",cmd_status,", sdec_(eCmd), ",armed,", sdec_(armedTicks))

PRI testT0_10() | pinAdcX, xNodeCounts
' C-6b: pin_adc_x_i (base+3) falls inside adc_pins, so the driver already
' samples it as a calibrated, frame-locked ADC every cycle -- it is simply
' never read. Start the REAL driver (rail must be on for this one test) so the
' fourth channel is live, then read it with RQPIN so this harness never steals
' the driver's own acknowledge on a pin the driver cog rdpin's every cycle.
' Commanded speed stays at zero (start() calls setTargetAccel(0) before the
' cog launches), so nothing turns.
'
' start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single top-level trap.
'
' @local pinAdcX - pinbase + 3, the X-node ADC pin
' @local xNodeCounts - RQPIN()'s lower 31 bits (bit 31 is the pin's C flag)

    debug("T0-10,begin,rail_must_be_on,TRUE")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    ' The reading is not gated on start()'s return (AD+: a start whose return read 0 once ran a real cog).
    ' AD+ is fixed and R1-T0-START certifies the return, so the start_return print is retired (task 3574).
    waitms(50)                                              ' let the driver cog reach its running, calibrated state
    pinAdcX := T0_MOTOR_BASE + 3
    xNodeCounts := RQPIN(pinAdcX) & $7FFF_FFFF
    debug("T0-10,end,pin,", udec_(pinAdcX), ",x_node_counts,", udec_(xNodeCounts))
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15bStart() : startResult, rawMotorCog
' R1-T0-EXHAUST (task 3499), the start: runExhaustionPhase() holds every free cog, so the real start()
' must fail. start() is called UNTRAPPED (task 3539): under total cog exhaustion it returns -1
' gracefully, which is NOT an abort; a genuine abort is caught by main()'s single top-level trap.
'
' @returns startResult - start()'s return under total cog exhaustion
' @returns rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the failed start()

    debug("T0-15,begin,exhaust")
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    rawMotorCog := motor.testGetMotorCog()
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()

PRI testT0_15bJudge(cogsOccupied, baseline, startResult, rawMotorCog, freeAfter) | bPass
' R1-T0-EXHAUST (task 3499), design SS H.1: runs LAST (runExhaustionPhase()). Count free cogs
' (baseline), occupy every free cog, call the real start(), release the spacers, count free cogs again.
' A BOOL cell (task 3537): measured is TRUE only when start() returns -1 AND testGetMotorCog() == 0 AND
' free cogs after release == baseline, so the suite is never left short a cog; the raw numbers are on
' the T0-15b line.
'
' @param cogsOccupied - spacers that held every free cog across the start
' @param baseline - free cogs before the occupancy
' @param startResult - start()'s return under total cog exhaustion
' @param rawMotorCog - testGetMotorCog()'s snapshot after the failed start()
' @param freeAfter - free cogs after every spacer is released

' Local Variables:
' @local bPass - this cell's measured value and verdict

    bPass := (startResult == SF_EXHAUST_LO) and (rawMotorCog == 0) and (freeAfter == baseline)
    debug("T0-15b,cogs_occupied,", udec_(cogsOccupied), ",start_return,", sdec_(startResult), ",raw_motor_cog,", sdec_(rawMotorCog), ",baseline,", udec_(baseline), ",free_after,", udec_(freeAfter))
    debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,R1-T0-EXHAUST,task,3499,motor,NONE,crit,RET_NEG_NOLEAK,measured,", zstr_(bPass ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",lo,TRUE,hi,TRUE,units,BOOL,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))

#ifdef T0_HAND
PRI testT0_12() | keyCode, bArmed, hallPin, hallCode, priorCode, transitions, illegalCount, pollIdx, pos
' T0-12, hand-rotation anchor -- SEPARABLE, compiled only under -D T0_HAND
' (its own bench-run.sh tier, t0-hand), so the unattended T0 run never waits
' on a person. The operator presses S, turns the right wheel by hand exactly
' T0_12_REVOLUTIONS revolutions in the direction T0_12_TOLD_CCW names, then
' presses SPACE; no other key starts or stops the count. It anchors 90 hall transitions per revolution and
' 5.763 mm/tick (isp_bldc_motor.spin2 hall tics per rotation, and
' DOCs/plans/VISIT-SIGNOFF-DESIGN.md SS A.5-b), and, per PL-39, ties the
' instructed direction to the sign of the tick change and the hall sequence
' observed. No sign-off cell -- confirmed against
' DOCs/analyses/bench/SIGNOFF-MANIFEST.tsv, which carries no T0-12 row; this
' is an operator-attended reference measurement, not a graded cell.
'
' No driver cog runs here, so the driver-maintained tick count
' (getRawHallTicks() reads the driver's pos) cannot move. This harness counts
' the transitions itself: it reads the three hall inputs (base+5..base+7)
' with pinread() every T0_12_POLL_MS. They are plain inputs -- nothing ever
' raises their DIR (task 3524) -- not smart pins, so pinread() is safe and no
' RDPIN is involved. Any change of the 3-bit code counts as one transition,
' and entering an illegal code (%000 or %111, symmetric under any bit order)
' is also counted separately. At a 1 ms poll a hand turn would need more than
' 5 revolutions per second (450 transitions per second, one every ~2.2 ms)
' before two transitions could fall between polls. `pos` accumulates the
' signed delta from t0hHallDeltas65 on every transition (PL-39); the table's
' own construction contributes 0 for any transition touching an illegal code,
' so no separate guard is needed.
'
' The pc_key() keypress-read pattern (own backtick, last in its debug()
' statement, ~100 ms poll matching PC_KEY's own latch window) already follows
' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7.
' The panel draws via the same doc's SS2-SS6 LAYER/CROP/UPDATE technique
' (t0hSetupPanel(), t0hDrawPanel()) from the committed assets
' tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py writes; rendering is shown only on the rig.
'
' @local keyCode - pc_key()'s last-read key code, 0 when none is latched
' @local bArmed - TRUE once a 0 reading has been seen (so a held key cannot register twice)
' @local hallPin - base+5, the lowest of the three hall inputs
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's 3-bit hall code
' @local transitions - hall code changes counted since the start keypress
' @local illegalCount - entries into %000 or %111 since the start keypress
' @local pollIdx - polls since the start keypress, paces the key checks, progress lines and redraws
' @local pos - signed tick position accumulated from t0hHallDeltas65 (PL-39)

    t0hSetupPanel()
    t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_WAITING, 0, 0)
    debug("T0-12,begin,told_direction,", zstr_(T0_12_TOLD_CCW ? @"CCW_FROM_HUB" : @"CW_FROM_HUB"), ",revolutions,", udec_(T0_12_REVOLUTIONS), ",wheel,RIGHT_P16,prompt,press_S_then_turn_the_wheel_by_hand_then_press_SPACE")

    hallPin := T0_MOTOR_BASE + T0_12_HALL_OFFSET

    bArmed := FALSE
    repeat
        debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))
        if keyCode == 0
            bArmed := TRUE
        if bArmed and ((keyCode == T0_12_KEY_START) or (keyCode == T0_12_KEY_START_LC))
            quit
        waitms(T0_12_KEY_WAIT_MS)

    priorCode := pinread(hallPin addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)
    transitions := 0
    illegalCount := 0
    pollIdx := 0
    pos := 0
    t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_COUNTING, transitions, illegalCount)
    debug("T0-12,started,hall_pin,", udec_(hallPin), ",hall_code,", udec_(priorCode), ",told_direction,", zstr_(T0_12_TOLD_CCW ? @"CCW_FROM_HUB" : @"CW_FROM_HUB"), ",prompt,press_SPACE_to_stop_count")

    bArmed := FALSE
    repeat
        hallCode := pinread(hallPin addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            transitions += 1
            if (hallCode == %000) or (hallCode == %111)
                illegalCount += 1
            pos += t0hHallDeltas65[(priorCode << 3) | hallCode] SIGNX 7    ' BYTE reads 0..255; SIGNX 7 gives -1/0/+1
            priorCode := hallCode
        pollIdx += 1
        if (pollIdx +// T0_12_KEY_POLLS) == 0
            debug(`bench `pc_key(@keyCode))
            if keyCode == 0
                bArmed := TRUE
            if bArmed and (keyCode == T0_12_KEY_STOP)
                quit
        if (pollIdx +// T0_12_PRINT_POLLS) == 0
            debug("T0-12,running,transitions,", udec_(transitions), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount), ",pos,", sdec_(pos))
            t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_COUNTING, transitions, illegalCount)
        waitms(T0_12_POLL_MS)

    t0hDrawPanel(T0H_STATE_DONE, transitions, illegalCount)
    debug("T0-12,end,transitions,", udec_(transitions), ",illegal,", udec_(illegalCount), ",pos,", sdec_(pos), ",final_hall_code,", udec_(priorCode), ",told_direction,", zstr_(T0_12_TOLD_CCW ? @"CCW_FROM_HUB" : @"CW_FROM_HUB"), ",note,expect_90_per_revolution_(5.763_mm_per_tick)")

PRI t0hSetupPanel()
' Create the T0-12 panel window and load its layers -- crop-and-overlay technique,
' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2 and SS6 step 4,
' as drawn on this bench by test_bench_char.spin2's since-removed panel
' (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/debug_260912-153807.log:19, LAYER/CROP 1/UPDATE sequence).
' Layer numbers and geometry are the T0H_* CON constants tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py also prints;
' the two must stay in sync (same discipline as tools/gen_bench_char_assets.py).
'
' The assets t0h_bg.bmp, t0h_state.bmp and t0h_digits.bmp are generated by
' `python3 tools/gen_t0hand_assets.py` and committed beside this file.

    debug(`PLOT bench TITLE 'T0-12 hand-rotation anchor' SIZE 420 240 POS 60 80 HIDEXY UPDATE)
    debug(`bench LAYER 1 't0h_bg.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 2 't0h_state.bmp')
    debug(`bench LAYER 3 't0h_digits.bmp')
    debug(`bench crop 1)
    debug(`bench update)

PRI t0hDrawPanel(stateIdx, transitions, illegalCount) | divisor, digitVal, destX, colIdx
' Compose one panel frame -- state word, transitions readout, illegal readout -- then one
' UPDATE (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2, "batch all crops, then one update"). Called
' only at each state change and every T0_12_PRINT_POLLS polls (~500 ms) from testT0_12()'s
' counting loop -- far below the 1 ms hall-poll rate, so it cannot starve pinread() polling.
'
' @param stateIdx - T0H_STATE_WAITING / T0H_STATE_COUNTING / T0H_STATE_DONE
' @param transitions - hall-code-change count to render (T0H_TRANS_COUNT digits, leading-zero suppressed)
' @param illegalCount - illegal-code-entry count to render (T0H_ILL_COUNT digits, leading-zero suppressed)
' @local divisor - selects the digit column currently being extracted (1000, 100, 10, 1, ...)
' @local digitVal - the digit value 0..9 for the current column
' @local destX - destination X for the current column's blit
' @local colIdx - loop index (digit column, most-significant first)

    debug(`bench crop 2 `(0, stateIdx * T0H_STATE_H, T0H_STATE_W, T0H_STATE_H, T0H_STATE_X, T0H_STATE_Y))

    divisor := 1000
    repeat colIdx from 0 to T0H_TRANS_COUNT - 1
        destX := T0H_TRANS_X + (colIdx * T0H_TRANS_PITCH)
        if (divisor == 1) or (transitions >= divisor)
            digitVal := (transitions / divisor) // 10
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(digitVal * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_TRANS_Y))
        else
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(T0H_DGT_BLANK * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_TRANS_Y))
        divisor /= 10

    divisor := 100
    repeat colIdx from 0 to T0H_ILL_COUNT - 1
        destX := T0H_ILL_X + (colIdx * T0H_ILL_PITCH)
        if (divisor == 1) or (illegalCount >= divisor)
            digitVal := (illegalCount / divisor) // 10
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(digitVal * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_ILL_Y))
        else
            debug(`bench crop 3 `(T0H_DGT_BLANK * T0H_DGT_W, 0, T0H_DGT_W, T0H_DGT_H, destX, T0H_ILL_Y))
        divisor /= 10

    debug(`bench update)
#endif

#ifdef T0_STOPMODE
PRI testT0_24() | rowIdx, startResult, bReady
' T0-24, stop-state hand test -- SEPARABLE, compiled only under -D T0_STOPMODE (its own
' bench-run.sh tier, t0-stopmode), so the unattended T0 run never waits on a person and never
' drives a motor. It is the run-time proof owed by task 3568 (DOCs/plans/STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md
' SS5, PL-89): the driver now names one bridge state per stop path, and only a hand on the wheel
' can say which state the hardware actually reached.
'
' SIX ROWS, in this order, each on the RIGHT wheel (T0_MOTOR_BASE):
'   1 HOLD AT REST      holdAtStop(TRUE) + stopMotor()   predicted BR_DRIVE, a powered hold
'   2 COAST AT REST     holdAtStop(FALSE) + stopMotor()  predicted BR_COAST, a freewheel
'   3 E-STOP AT REST    emergencyCutoff()                predicted BR_SHORT, a dynamic brake
'   4 FAULT, COAST MODE a provoked fault under SM_FLOAT  predicted BR_COAST
'   5 FAULT, HOLD MODE  a provoked fault under SM_BRAKE  predicted BR_SHORT
'   6 DRIVER COG STOPPED stop()                          the pins released: the free yardstick
' Row 6 is last because stop() ends the driver cog; rows 4 and 5 are the only ones that drive.
'
' WHY ROW 3 ALSO ANSWERS "DID THE OLD BUILD BRAKE IN FLOAT?" (the task's owed decision, and
' STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS7's open question, settled here BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by a run of
' the pre-88294d5 binary). BR_SHORT is written as `wypin #0, drive_pins` on all six pins -- the
' identical instruction the old `driveoff = 1` path ran for FLOAT at rest. So row 3 measures, on
' the fixed binary, the very state the old build put a floated wheel into. No second binary is
' built, no bench time is spent on one, and the release note is worded from row 3's reading.
'
' WHY THE OPERATOR NEVER JUDGES A ROW (overlay P7). His key press sequences the row and marks the
' moment he lets go; it is an input, not an opinion, and no cell reads it. Every verdict comes
' from the hall counter in t0sProbe() and from the driver's own state.
'
' @local rowIdx - the row being run, T0_24_ROW_*
' @local startResult - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver came up ready, so the rows can run at all

    t0sSetupPanel()
    t0sDrawPanel(T0_24_ROW_HOLD, T0_24_ACT_SETUP, 0, 0, 0)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellHoldPwr, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellRestCoast, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellRestShort, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellStopGap, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFltCoast, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFltShort, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFltGap, @sTaskStopMode)
    emitCellDecl(@sCellFreeRef, @sTaskStopMode)
    debug("T0-24,begin,wheel,RIGHT_P16,rows,", udec_(T0_24_ROW_COUNT), ",fault_power,", udec_(T0_24_FLT_POWER), ",prompt,each_row_names_what_to_do_on_the_panel_before_it_runs")

    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    startResult := motor.start(T0_MOTOR_BASE, user.DRIVE_VOLTAGE, motor.BRD_AUTO_DET)
    benchLog.cogEventEnd()
    bReady := bWaitReady(startResult)
    if bReady
        repeat rowIdx from 0 to T0_24_ROW_COUNT - 1
            t0sRunRow(rowIdx)
    else
        debug("T0-24,not_ready,start_result,", sdec_(startResult), ",note,every_cell_is_NOMEAS")
    t0sEmitCells()
    t0sDrawPanel(T0_24_ROW_ALLDONE, T0_24_ACT_ALLDONE, 0, 0, 0)
    benchLog.cogEventBegin()
    motor.stop()                                                ' row 6 already stopped it on a full run; harmless twice,
    motor.getError()                                            '  and it is the only release on the not-ready path
    debug("T0-24,end")

PRI t0sRunRow(rowIdx) | actionIdx, handTicks, afterTicks, afterMs, halfMs, releaseSpan, protCode, bSetUp
' Run one row end to end: announce it, wait to be armed, build the state, measure the hand, and
' print the row's record. Nothing here judges: t0sEmitCells() does that once, at the end, because
' three of the cells compare one row with another.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
'
' @local actionIdx - the action cell this row asks for, T0_24_ACT_TURNSLOW or T0_24_ACT_SPIN
' @local handTicks - hall ticks while his hand was on the wheel
' @local afterTicks - hall ticks after he let go
' @local afterMs - how long those took
' @local halfMs - ms from the release to half the release rate: this row's criterion
' @local releaseSpan - the six-tick span at the moment he let go, ms; 0 when there was no release rate
' @local protCode - getProtectiveStop()'s code, read once for the row's record
' @local bSetUp - TRUE when the row's stop state was actually reached

    releaseSpan := 0                                            ' the row's record prints it even when the row never ran
    t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, T0_24_ACT_ARM, 0, 0, 0)
    debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(rowIdx), ",arm,prediction,", zstr_(t0sRowPrediction(rowIdx)), ",asking_for,", zstr_(t0sRowAction(rowIdx)), ",prompt,press_S_when_ready")
    t0sWaitArm()
    if (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD)
        t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, T0_24_ACT_POWERED, 0, 0, 0)        ' the panel says the wheel is about to spin BEFORE it does,
    else                                                        '  and says so for as long as it is spinning (overlay P1)
        t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, T0_24_ACT_SETUP, 0, 0, 0)
    bSetUp := bT0sSetUpRow(rowIdx)
    if bSetUp
        if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLD                             ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
            actionIdx := T0_24_ACT_TURNSLOW
        else
            actionIdx := T0_24_ACT_SPIN
        handTicks, afterTicks, afterMs, halfMs, releaseSpan := t0sProbe(rowIdx, actionIdx)
        t0sHandTicks[rowIdx] := handTicks
        t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx] := afterTicks
        t0sAfterMs[rowIdx] := afterMs
        t0sHalfMs[rowIdx] := halfMs
        bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] := (handTicks >= SF_HAND_MIN_TICKS) and (releaseSpan > 0)
        if (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST) or (rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD)
            bT0sStillFaulted[rowIdx] := (motor.getDriverState() == motor.DCS_FAULTED)
        if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLD
            bT0sHoldFaulted := motor.isFaultSignal()            ' the hold is powered exactly when turning it faults
    else
        bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] := FALSE
    protCode := motor.getProtectiveStop()
    debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(rowIdx), ",set_up,", zstr_(bSetUp ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",hand_ticks,", udec_(t0sHandTicks[rowIdx]), ",after_ticks,", udec_(t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx]), ",after_ms,", udec_(t0sAfterMs[rowIdx]), ",half_ms,", udec_(t0sHalfMs[rowIdx]), ",release_span_ms,", udec_(releaseSpan), ",still_faulted,", zstr_(bT0sStillFaulted[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"), ",protective,", sdec_(protCode), ",measured,", zstr_(bT0sRowMeasured[rowIdx] ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    t0sTearDownRow(rowIdx)
    t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, T0_24_ACT_ROWDONE, t0sHandTicks[rowIdx], t0sAfterTicks[rowIdx], t0sAfterMs[rowIdx])

PRI bT0sSetUpRow(rowIdx) : bSetUp
' Put the driver into this row's stop state, and report whether it got there.
'
' A stop state is only what the DRIVER is in, so each row checks the driver rather than assuming
' the call took: the e-stop row reads isEmergency(), the two fault rows require the provoked fault.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @returns bSetUp - TRUE when the row's state was reached

    bSetUp := FALSE
    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLD:
            motor.clearFaultSignal()                            ' the row's own criterion is a fault recorded FROM HERE
            motor.holdAtStop(TRUE)
            motor.stopMotor()
            waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
            bSetUp := (motor.isFaultSignal() == FALSE)
        T0_24_ROW_COAST:
            motor.holdAtStop(FALSE)
            motor.stopMotor()
            waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
            bSetUp := TRUE
        T0_24_ROW_ESTOP:
            motor.emergencyCutoff()
            waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
            bSetUp := motor.isEmergency()
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST:
            bSetUp := bT0sProvoke(FALSE)
        T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:
            bSetUp := bT0sProvoke(TRUE)
        T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP:
            benchLog.cogEventBegin()
            motor.stop()
            waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
            bSetUp := TRUE

PRI t0sTearDownRow(rowIdx)
' Leave the driver ready for the next row. Nothing here runs before the row's reading is taken:
' every one of these calls would itself change the bridge state the row just measured.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row just finished, T0_24_ROW_*

    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLD:
            motor.clearFaultSignal()
        T0_24_ROW_ESTOP:
            motor.clearEmergency()
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST:
            motor.clearFaultSignal()                            ' the driver itself leaves DCS_FAULTED on the next row's
            motor.clearProtectiveStop()                         '  first command (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:1124)
        T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:
            motor.clearFaultSignal()
            motor.clearProtectiveStop()
        other:
            motor.getError()                                    ' the rows that need no teardown still drain the error slot

PRI bT0sProvoke(bHold) : bFaulted | negOfs, posOfs, shiftDeg, bAtSpeed
' Rows 4 and 5: fault the driver at speed under the stop mode bHold selects, then let the wheel
' come to rest with the fault still in force.
'
' THE PROVOCATION IS COMPUTED, NOT CHOSEN (R17.5, PL-86/PL-59, ported from the dual harness's
' faultShiftDeg()): an offset written at rest is absorbed by the start's re-seed and the lag
' limiter, and the wheel then draws ~16 A without ever faulting. Driven at speed, shifting both
' offsets by exactly what moves this wheel's own position error onto the |err| >= 125 test faults
' it in the NEXT control frame, before any current can build.
'
' NOTHING IS COMMANDED AFTER THE FAULT. The driver leaves DCS_FAULTED as soon as a stop or a
' different power is commanded (isp_bldc_motor.spin2:1124), and leaving it re-runs checkstop --
' which would replace the fault's bridge state with the at-rest one and measure the wrong thing.
' So the coast to rest here is a wait, not a stop.
'
' @param bHold - TRUE selects SM_BRAKE (predicted BR_SHORT on the fault), FALSE SM_FLOAT (BR_COAST)
' @returns bFaulted - TRUE when the driver faulted and the wheel then reached rest
'
' @local negOfs - the offset applied to negative increments, read before the shift and put back after
' @local posOfs - the offset applied to positive increments
' @local shiftDeg - the computed shift, degrees
' @local bAtSpeed - TRUE when the wheel reached AT_SPEED inside the bound

    bFaulted := FALSE
    motor.holdAtStop(bHold)
    motor.driveAtPower(T0_24_FLT_POWER)
    bAtSpeed := bT0sWaitDriver(T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED, T0_24_SPEED_MS)
    if bAtSpeed
        waitms(T0_24_SETTLE_MS)
        negOfs, posOfs := motor.testGetFwdRevIndep()
        shiftDeg := t0sFaultShiftDeg()
        motor.testSetFwdRevIndep(negOfs + shiftDeg, posOfs + shiftDeg)
        bFaulted := bT0sWaitDriver(T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT, T0_24_NO_FAULT_MS)
        motor.testSetFwdRevIndep(negOfs, posOfs)                ' put them back on EVERY path that wrote them
        debug("T0-24,provoke,hold_mode,", zstr_(bHold ? @"BRAKE" : @"FLOAT"), ",offset_neg,", udec_(negOfs), ",offset_pos,", udec_(posOfs), ",shift_deg,", udec_(shiftDeg), ",faulted,", zstr_(bFaulted ? @"TRUE" : @"FALSE"))
    else
        debug("T0-24,provoke,hold_mode,", zstr_(bHold ? @"BRAKE" : @"FLOAT"), ",why,NOT_AT_SPEED,note,no_offset_was_written")
    if bFaulted
        t0sWaitRest()
    else
        motor.stopMotor()                                       ' no fault to preserve, so the wheel is stopped at once

PRI t0sFaultShiftDeg() : shiftDeg | sampleIdx, errSum, errMean, shiftUnits
' The commutation-offset shift that puts this wheel's position error on the driver's fault test.
'
' The driver's err is one electrical cycle in T0_24_ERR_PER_TURN signed units, so it wraps at
' +-128, and it faults at |err| >= 125. err = field angle - (hall angle + offset), and the offset
' maps positively, so raising the offset by D units lowers err by D in the next control frame.
' D = err + T0_24_ERR_TARGET lands the error on the wrap: any landing 125..131 away faults, which
' is +-3 units of margin against the 1-degree offset resolution.
'
' @returns shiftDeg - the shift to add to both of this wheel's offsets, degrees
'
' @local sampleIdx - read counter
' @local errSum - sum of the reads
' @local errMean - the wheel's mean position error at speed, err units
' @local shiftUnits - the shift, err units

    errSum := 0
    repeat sampleIdx from 1 to T0_24_ERR_SAMPLES
        errSum += t0sWheelErr()
        waitms(T0_24_SAMPLE_MS)
    errMean := errSum / T0_24_ERR_SAMPLES
    shiftUnits := (errMean + T0_24_ERR_TARGET) & T0_24_ERR_MASK
    shiftDeg := ((shiftUnits * T0_24_DEG_PER_TURN) + (T0_24_ERR_PER_TURN / 2)) / T0_24_ERR_PER_TURN

PRI t0sWheelErr() : nErr
' This wheel's latest position error from the driver's status block.
'
' @returns nErr - the error, signed err units

    _, nErr, _, _, _, _, _, _ := motor.testGetTelemetry()

PRI bT0sWaitDriver(untilKind, boundMs) : bReached | waitedMs, sampleIdx, bEnded
' The one bounded wait a powered window uses, for either state it ever waits on. The absolute
' current abort and the operator's SPACE are live throughout, and either stops the motor, so the
' caller's next act is never to drive further.
'
' @param untilKind - T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED or T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT: the driver state being waited on
' @param boundMs - the wait's bound; reaching it is not an abort, it is the state not arriving
' @returns bReached - TRUE when the state arrived inside the bound with nothing aborting
'
' @local waitedMs - wait accumulator
' @local sampleIdx - samples since the last key check, pacing it to the panel's ~100 ms cadence
' @local bEnded - TRUE once the wait is over, however it ended

    bReached := FALSE
    bEnded := FALSE
    waitedMs := 0
    sampleIdx := 0
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        if bT0sDriverAt(untilKind)
            bReached := TRUE
            bEnded := TRUE
        elseif bT0sPoweredAbort(sampleIdx)
            bEnded := TRUE
        elseif waitedMs >= boundMs
            bEnded := TRUE
        else
            waitms(T0_24_SAMPLE_MS)
            waitedMs += T0_24_SAMPLE_MS
            sampleIdx += 1

PRI bT0sDriverAt(untilKind) : bThere
' Report whether the driver is in the state a wait is waiting on.
'
' @param untilKind - T0_24_UNTIL_SPEED or T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT
' @returns bThere - TRUE when the driver is in that state now

    if untilKind == T0_24_UNTIL_FAULT                           ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        bThere := motor.isFaulted()
    else
        bThere := (motor.getDriverState() == motor.DCS_AT_SPEED)

PRI bT0sPoweredAbort(sampleIdx) : bAbort | amps, keyCode
' The two live aborts of a powered window: the absolute current ceiling, read every sample, and
' the operator's SPACE, read at the panel's own ~100 ms cadence. Either stops the motor here, so
' the caller's next act is never to drive further.
'
' @param sampleIdx - the caller's sample counter, which paces the key read
' @returns bAbort - TRUE when the powered window must end now
'
' @local amps - getCurrent()'s reading, 0.1 mA units
' @local keyCode - t0sReadKey()'s reading, 0 when no key is latched

    bAbort := FALSE
    amps, _ := motor.getCurrent()
    if abs(amps) >= T0_24_ABORT_AMPS
        bAbort := TRUE
        debug("T0-24,abort,why,ABS_CURRENT,amps_x10k,", sdec_(amps))
    elseif (sampleIdx +// T0_24_KEY_SAMPLES) == 0
        keyCode := t0sReadKey()                                 ' no arm-latch here: SPACE is a live abort for as long as
        if keyCode == T0_24_KEY_STOP                            '  the wheel is powered, not a wait ended by a rising edge
            bAbort := TRUE
            debug("T0-24,abort,why,OPERATOR_SPACE")
    if bAbort
        motor.stopMotor()

PRI t0sWaitRest() | quietMs, waitedMs, hallCode, priorCode, bEnded
' Wait for the wheel to stop turning after a provoked fault, bounded by T0_24_REST_WAIT_MS, by
' watching the hall inputs and nothing else. Rest is T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS with no transition.
' Commands nothing: see bT0sProvoke()'s note on why a stop here would erase the state.
'
' @local quietMs - ms since the last hall transition
' @local waitedMs - total wait
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's code
' @local bEnded - TRUE once at rest or out of budget

    priorCode := t0sHallCode()
    quietMs := 0
    waitedMs := 0
    bEnded := FALSE
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        hallCode := t0sHallCode()
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            priorCode := hallCode
            quietMs := 0
        else
            quietMs += T0_24_POLL_MS
        waitedMs += T0_24_POLL_MS
        bEnded := (quietMs >= T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS) or (waitedMs >= T0_24_REST_WAIT_MS)
        waitms(T0_24_POLL_MS)
    debug("T0-24,at_rest,waited_ms,", udec_(waitedMs), ",driver_state,", udec_(motor.getDriverState()))

PRI t0sProbe(rowIdx, actionIdx) : handTicks, afterTicks, afterMs, halfMs, releaseSpan | bArmed, hallCode, priorCode, pollIdx, nowMs, keyMs, startMs, tickMs[T0_24_TICK_RING], ringIdx, tickCount, lastTickMs, spanNow, bEnded
' The measurement every row shares: what the wheel does under a hand, counted by this harness's
' own hall poll (T0-12's proven loop and its hand-maintained delta table's pin set) so that rows
' with a driver cog running and row 6, which has none, are measured by the identical instrument.
'
' TWO PHASES. While his hand is on the wheel the poll counts hall transitions and keeps the last
' T0_24_TICK_RING tick timestamps. SPACE marks the release: the span of those six ticks is the
' RELEASE RATE. The second phase counts what the wheel does with nobody touching it, and reports
' the ms until the six-tick span has doubled -- the time to fall to half the release rate.
'
' WHY HALF-RATE TIME AND NOT DISTANCE. How far the wheel carries on scales with however hard he
' pushed, so a fixed tick limit would be a reading about his arm. A shorted winding brakes with a
' torque proportional to speed, so the time to halve is a property of the bridge state and not of
' the push -- which is what the cells judge. The distance is printed beside it all the same.
'
' The pc_key() pattern (own backtick, last in its debug() statement, ~100 ms poll matching
' PC_KEY's latch window) follows DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/
' DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7, as T0-12 does.
'
' @param rowIdx - the row being measured, for the panel
' @param actionIdx - the action cell this row asks for
' @returns handTicks - hall ticks while his hand was on the wheel
' @returns afterTicks - hall ticks after he let go
' @returns afterMs - ms from the release to the last tick
' @returns halfMs - ms from the release to half the release rate, or the whole coast when it never halved
' @returns releaseSpan - the six-tick span at the release, ms; 0 when there was no release rate to take
'
' @local bArmed - TRUE once a 0 reading has been seen, so a held key cannot register twice
' @local hallCode - the 3-bit hall code just read
' @local priorCode - the previous poll's code
' @local pollIdx - polls since the phase began, paces the key checks and redraws
' @local nowMs - this poll's getms()
' @local keyMs - getms() at the release
' @local startMs - getms() at the phase start, for the hand-phase cap
' @local tickMs - the last T0_24_TICK_RING tick timestamps
' @local ringIdx - where the next tick's timestamp goes, and so the oldest kept
' @local tickCount - ticks seen in both phases, so the ring is known to be full
' @local lastTickMs - getms() at the last transition: ends the release-rate span, and times the rest test
' @local spanNow - the six-tick span at the tick just counted, ms
' @local bEnded - TRUE once the current phase is over

    t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, actionIdx, 0, 0, 0)
    debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(rowIdx), ",hand_phase,begin,asking_for,", zstr_(t0sRowAction(rowIdx)))
    priorCode := t0sHallCode()
    handTicks := 0
    tickCount := 0
    ringIdx := 0
    pollIdx := 0
    bArmed := FALSE
    bEnded := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    lastTickMs := startMs
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        hallCode := t0sHallCode()
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            handTicks += 1
            tickCount += 1
            lastTickMs := getms()
            tickMs[ringIdx] := lastTickMs
            ringIdx := (ringIdx + 1) +// T0_24_TICK_RING
            priorCode := hallCode
        pollIdx += 1
        if (pollIdx +// T0_24_KEY_POLLS) == 0
            bEnded := bT0sLatchedKey(@bArmed, T0_24_KEY_STOP, T0_24_KEY_STOP)
        if (pollIdx +// T0_24_PRINT_POLLS) == 0
            t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, actionIdx, handTicks, 0, 0)
        if (getms() - startMs) >= T0_24_HAND_CAP_MS
            bEnded := TRUE
        waitms(T0_24_POLL_MS)

    keyMs := getms()
    releaseSpan := 0
    if tickCount >= T0_24_TICK_RING
        releaseSpan := lastTickMs - tickMs[ringIdx]             ' ringIdx now holds the OLDEST of the last six, and the span
                                                                '  ends at the last TICK, so his reaction time is not in it
    t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, T0_24_ACT_COASTING, handTicks, 0, 0)
    debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(rowIdx), ",released,hand_ticks,", udec_(handTicks), ",release_span_ms,", udec_(releaseSpan))

    afterTicks := 0
    halfMs := -1
    lastTickMs := keyMs
    pollIdx := 0
    bEnded := FALSE
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        hallCode := t0sHallCode()
        nowMs := getms()
        if hallCode <> priorCode
            afterTicks += 1
            tickCount += 1
            spanNow := nowMs - tickMs[ringIdx]                  ' the span of the six ticks ending at this one
            tickMs[ringIdx] := nowMs
            ringIdx := (ringIdx + 1) +// T0_24_TICK_RING
            priorCode := hallCode
            lastTickMs := nowMs
            if (halfMs < 0) and (releaseSpan > 0) and (spanNow >= (releaseSpan * T0_24_HALF_FACTOR))
                halfMs := nowMs - keyMs
        pollIdx += 1
        if (pollIdx +// T0_24_PRINT_POLLS) == 0
            t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, T0_24_ACT_COASTING, handTicks, afterTicks, nowMs - keyMs)
        bEnded := ((nowMs - lastTickMs) >= T0_24_REST_QUIET_MS) or ((nowMs - keyMs) >= T0_24_COAST_CAP_MS)
        waitms(T0_24_POLL_MS)

    afterMs := (lastTickMs - keyMs) #> 0
    if halfMs < 0
        halfMs := afterMs                                       ' it stopped before the rate ever halved: the whole coast
    debug("T0-24,row,", udec_(rowIdx), ",coast,after_ticks,", udec_(afterTicks), ",after_ms,", udec_(afterMs), ",half_ms,", udec_(halfMs))

PRI t0sReadKey() : keyCode
' The panel's keyboard, read once. Every key this tier reads comes through here, so the debug
' record that carries pc_key() is written ONE time: a literal debug() format string costs about
' 150 bytes of this binary's DEBUG data budget, which is the same reason emitCellBool() and
' t0sEmitNum() exist.
'
' The backtick call is last in its debug() statement, as PC_KEY requires
' (DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS7).
'
' @returns keyCode - the key code latched since the last read, 0 when none is

    keyCode := 0
    debug(`t0stop `pc_key(@keyCode))

PRI bT0sLatchedKey(pArmed, keyWanted, keyAlso) : bHit | keyCode
' Report whether one of two wanted keys has been pressed SINCE THE WAIT BEGAN. A key is only
' honoured once a 0 reading has been seen, so a key still held from the previous wait cannot end
' this one too -- which is why the caller owns the armed flag and passes it in.
'
' @param pArmed - pointer to the caller''s armed flag, set TRUE by the first 0 reading
' @param keyWanted - the key that ends the wait
' @param keyAlso - a second accepted key; pass keyWanted again when there is only one
' @returns bHit - TRUE when an armed, wanted key has been read
'
' @local keyCode - this read''s key code

    keyCode := t0sReadKey()
    if keyCode == 0
        LONG[pArmed] := TRUE
    bHit := (LONG[pArmed] <> FALSE) and ((keyCode == keyWanted) or (keyCode == keyAlso))

PRI t0sWaitArm() | bArmed, bEnded
' Wait for S (either case) before a row's state is built, so nothing happens while he is still
' walking back to the rig. No other key arms a row.
'
' @local bArmed - TRUE once a 0 reading has been seen, so a held key cannot arm two rows
' @local bEnded - TRUE once S has been seen

    bArmed := FALSE
    bEnded := FALSE
    repeat while bEnded == FALSE
        bEnded := bT0sLatchedKey(@bArmed, T0_24_KEY_START, T0_24_KEY_START_LC)
        waitms(T0_24_KEY_WAIT_MS)

PRI t0sHallCode() : hallCode
' The three hall inputs as one 3-bit code. They are plain inputs -- nothing ever raises their DIR
' (task 3524) -- not smart pins, so pinread() is safe whether or not a driver cog is running.
'
' @returns hallCode - the 3-bit hall code

    hallCode := pinread((T0_MOTOR_BASE + T0_12_HALL_OFFSET) addpins T0_12_HALL_SPAN)

PRI t0sRowPrediction(rowIdx) : pText
' STOP-STATE-DESIGN.md SS5's prediction for a row, printed beside the row's own reading so the log
' carries what was expected before anyone reads what happened.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @returns pText - pointer to the prediction text

    case rowIdx
        T0_24_ROW_HOLD:     pText := @"HELD_AT_A_FIXED_ANGLE_COGGING_RESISTANCE_AND_A_RECORDED_FAULT_WHEN_TURNED"
        T0_24_ROW_COAST:    pText := @"SPINS_FREELY_AND_COASTS"
        T0_24_ROW_ESTOP:    pText := @"RESISTS_HARDER_THE_FASTER_IT_IS_TURNED"
        T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST: pText := @"SPINS_FREELY_AND_COASTS"
        T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD:  pText := @"RESISTS_HARDER_THE_FASTER_IT_IS_TURNED"
        other:              pText := @"SPINS_FREELY_THE_PINS_ARE_RELEASED"

PRI t0sRowAction(rowIdx) : pText
' What the operator is asked to do in this row, named in the log BEFORE the row runs and shown on
' the panel at the same moment (overlay P1: an observation nothing asked for is never requested
' afterwards).
'
' @param rowIdx - which row, T0_24_ROW_*
' @returns pText - pointer to the action text

    if rowIdx == T0_24_ROW_HOLD                                 ' if/else, never `? :` -- PL-29, PL-76
        pText := @"TURN_IT_SLOWLY_ABOUT_HALF_A_TURN_THEN_PRESS_SPACE"
    else
        pText := @"SPIN_IT_BRISKLY_LET_GO_AND_PRESS_SPACE_AS_YOU_LET_GO"

PRI t0sEmitCells() | coastGap, fltGap
' Every cell this tier judges, emitted once, after the last row: three of them compare two rows
' with each other and so cannot be judged where either row runs.
'
' @local coastGap - row 2's half-rate time less row 3's, ms
' @local fltGap - row 4's half-rate time less row 5's, ms

    emitCellBool(@sCellHoldPwr, @sTaskStopMode, @"RIGHT", @sCritHoldPwr, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_HOLD], bT0sHoldFaulted, 1)
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellRestCoast, @sCritRestCoast, t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_COAST], SF_FREE_HALF_MS, T0_24_COAST_CAP_MS, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COAST], t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_COAST] >= SF_FREE_HALF_MS)
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellRestShort, @sCritRestShort, t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP], 0, SF_BRAKE_HALF_MS, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP], t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP] <= SF_BRAKE_HALF_MS)
    coastGap := t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_COAST] - t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP]
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellStopGap, @sCritStopGap, coastGap, SF_MODE_GAP_MS, T0_24_COAST_CAP_MS, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COAST] and bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_ESTOP], coastGap >= SF_MODE_GAP_MS)
    emitCellBool(@sCellFltCoast, @sTaskStopMode, @"RIGHT", @sCritFltCoast, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST], (t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST] >= SF_FREE_HALF_MS) and bT0sStillFaulted[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST], 1)
    emitCellBool(@sCellFltShort, @sTaskStopMode, @"RIGHT", @sCritFltShort, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD], (t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD] <= SF_BRAKE_HALF_MS) and bT0sStillFaulted[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD], 1)
    fltGap := t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST] - t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD]
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellFltGap, @sCritFltGap, fltGap, SF_MODE_GAP_MS, T0_24_COAST_CAP_MS, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTCOAST] and bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_FLTHOLD], fltGap >= SF_MODE_GAP_MS)
    t0sEmitNum(@sCellFreeRef, @sCritFreeRef, t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP], SF_FREE_HALF_MS, T0_24_COAST_CAP_MS, bT0sRowMeasured[T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP], t0sHalfMs[T0_24_ROW_COGSTOP] >= SF_FREE_HALF_MS)

PRI t0sEmitNum(pCell, pCrit, measuredMs, loMs, hiMs, bMeasured, bPass)
' One numeric SIGNOFF for a T0-24 cell, in ms. The cell and criterion names are hub strings rather
' than literals inside the debug() call, so all five numeric cells share these two DEBUG records
' and their data (see emitCellBool() for the same reason).
'
' @param pCell - pointer to the cell id
' @param pCrit - pointer to the criterion token
' @param measuredMs - the reading
' @param loMs - the criterion's low limit
' @param hiMs - its high limit
' @param bMeasured - TRUE when the row was set up AND the wheel was actually turned
' @param bPass - the criterion held

    if bMeasured
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,3578,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,", sdec_(measuredMs), ",lo,", sdec_(loMs), ",hi,", sdec_(hiMs), ",units,MS,n,1,verdict,", zstr_(bPass ? @"PASS" : @"FAIL"))
    else
        debug("SIGNOFF,sf,1,bin,T0,cell,", zstr_(pCell), ",task,3578,motor,RIGHT,crit,", zstr_(pCrit), ",measured,NA,lo,", sdec_(loMs), ",hi,", sdec_(hiMs), ",units,MS,n,0,verdict,NOMEAS")

PRI t0sSetupPanel()
' Create the T0-24 panel window and load its layers -- crop-and-overlay technique,
' DOCs/REF-NO-COMMIT/dbg-display-theory/DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2 and SS6 step 4, as
' T0-12's own panel draws it on this rig. Layer numbers and geometry are the T0S_* CON constants
' tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py also prints; the two must stay in sync.
'
' The assets t0s_bg.bmp, t0s_rows.bmp, t0s_actions.bmp and t0s_digits.bmp are generated by
' `python3 tools/gen_t0stop_assets.py` and committed beside this file.

    debug(`PLOT t0stop TITLE 'T0-24 stop-state hand test' SIZE 480 300 POS 60 80 HIDEXY UPDATE)
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 1 't0s_bg.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 2 't0s_rows.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 3 't0s_actions.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop LAYER 4 't0s_digits.bmp')
    debug(`t0stop crop 1)
    debug(`t0stop update)

PRI t0sDrawPanel(rowIdx, actionIdx, handTicks, afterTicks, afterMs)
' Compose one panel frame -- the row, the action it is asking for, and the three readings -- then
' one UPDATE (DISPLAY-PATTERNS-builders-guide.md SS2, "batch all crops, then one update"). Called
' at each phase change and every T0_24_PRINT_POLLS polls (~500 ms), far below the 1 ms hall poll,
' so it cannot starve the counting.
'
' @param rowIdx - which row's name to show, T0_24_ROW_* or T0_24_ROW_ALLDONE
' @param actionIdx - which action to show, T0_24_ACT_*
' @param handTicks - the hand-phase reading to render
' @param afterTicks - the after-release tick reading
' @param afterMs - the after-release time reading

    debug(`t0stop crop 2 `(0, rowIdx * T0S_ROW_H, T0S_ROW_W, T0S_ROW_H, T0S_ROW_X, T0S_ROW_Y))
    debug(`t0stop crop 3 `(0, actionIdx * T0S_ACT_H, T0S_ACT_W, T0S_ACT_H, T0S_ACT_X, T0S_ACT_Y))
    t0sBlitNum(T0S_HAND_Y, handTicks, T0S_HAND_COUNT)
    t0sBlitNum(T0S_AFTER_Y, afterTicks, T0S_AFTER_COUNT)
    t0sBlitNum(T0S_MS_Y, afterMs, T0S_MS_COUNT)
    debug(`t0stop update)

PRI t0sBlitNum(destY, numValue, digitCount) | divisor, digitVal, destX, colIdx
' Blit one readout, most significant digit first, leading zeros suppressed.
'
' @param destY - the readout's row on the canvas
' @param numValue - the value to render
' @param digitCount - how many digit cells the readout has
'
' @local divisor - selects the digit column currently being extracted
' @local digitVal - the digit value 0..9 for the current column
' @local destX - destination X for the current column's blit
' @local colIdx - loop index (digit column, most significant first)

    divisor := 1
    repeat colIdx from 2 to digitCount
        divisor *= 10
    repeat colIdx from 0 to digitCount - 1
        destX := T0S_READ_X + (colIdx * T0S_READ_PITCH)
        if (divisor == 1) or (numValue >= divisor)
            digitVal := (numValue / divisor) +// 10
            debug(`t0stop crop 4 `(digitVal * T0S_DGT_W, 0, T0S_DGT_W, T0S_DGT_H, destX, destY))
        else
            debug(`t0stop crop 4 `(T0S_DGT_BLANK * T0S_DGT_W, 0, T0S_DGT_W, T0S_DGT_H, destX, destY))
        divisor /= 10
#endif

